{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011HotVGUiePKqyEf9cmCwW9","type":"tool_result","content":"420\t### 4.1 Rail3D, the renderer\n421\t**Data**\n422\t- **Mesh**: `{ groups: [{ mat, pos: Float32Array, nrm, uv, lit: Float32Array (baked light per vertex), flags }], bounds, sphere }`.\n423\t- **TextureBank** (built at boot):\n424\t  - each material has 5 band tiles: `E.materialTile(id, { size: 32, px: 2, band: 0..4 })`, plus `lid: true` versions\n425\t    for faces that look up or down. Each tile is converted to a `Uint32Array`.\n426\t  - Tiles are `v`-up with the top row first, so flip v when sampling.\n427\t  - Face-pattern materials (crate) use uv 0..1 across each face.\n428\t  - Use **named** materials in shape entries so `materialTile(id)` resolves them. Register any inline material in\n429\t    `E.MATERIALS` under a generated id first.\n430\t  - Material flags: `glow` (emissive), `water`, `double` (draw both sides), `alphaTest` (nets, grates, foliage cards,\n431\t    on the tile's alpha or a pattern mask), `scroll` (uv speed).\n432\t- **Instances**: `{ mesh, M (3×4), visible, dynamic, tint, flash, collider ids }`.\n433\t- **Static world**: built when a stage is built, then transformed to world space and baked. The baked light is\n434\t  `ambient + sunK·max(0, n·sun) + Σ static lights` plus contact darkening where a wall meets the floor. Tessellate\n435\t  faces to edges of 64 u or less so the vertex light, fog and near clipping stay clean. Bin it into 256-u chunks with\n436\t  bounding spheres for frustum culling.\n437\t\n438\t**Per viewport, per frame**\n439\t1. `begin(cam, rect)`: the basis, `F`, the frustum planes; clear the depth to `+∞`.\n440\t2. **Sky**, per pixel from the ray's elevation e and azimuth a:\n441\t   - a three-stop gradient (the stage palette);\n442\t   - stars from a hash of the quantized direction where e > 0.05, twinkling;\n443\t   - a moon or sun disc with a halo;\n444\t   - two octaves of drifting noise clouds;\n445\t   - one to three distant silhouette layers on the horizon (`h(a)` heightfields: skyline, cliffs, the barrier);\n446\t   - lightning brightens it.\n447\t3. **Triangles**, for each visible group:\n448\t   - transform to view space, clip against the near plane (z = 2 u; Sutherland–Hodgman, a triangle becomes 0–2),\n449\t     project, and cull back faces unless the material is `double`;\n450\t   - rasterize over the integer bounding box with edge functions and a top-left fill rule. Interpolate `1/z`, `u/z`,\n451\t     `v/z` and `L/z` for perspective-correct values;\n452\t   - depth test on view z;\n453\t   - per pixel: `band = clamp(floor(L·4 + bayer4[x&3][y&3]), 0, 4)` (the engine's banded light, dithered between\n454\t     bands) → texel → fog → write color and depth;\n455\t   - fog `f = clamp((z − near)/(far − near))^1.2`, quantized to 8 steps with the Bayer threshold. Emissive materials\n456\t     skip lighting and take half the fog.\n457\t   - *Retro wobble* (a setting, off by default) snaps vertices to whole pixels and makes texturing affine.\n458\t4. **Dynamic light** on top of the baked light: up to 12 point lights per frame (muzzle flashes, explosions, flares,\n459\t   the lighthouse beam, the tram's lamps). Each adds `k·(1 − d/r)²` per vertex, only for triangles whose bounding\n460\t   sphere it touches.\n461\t5. **Water**: a material with `water: true`.\n462\t   - The band comes from `base + 0.6·sin(u·.11 + t·1.3)·sin(v·.07 − t)` plus noise.\n463\t   - Sparkles: the `hi` color where noise(u + t·8, v) > 0.82, weighted toward the moon or sun direction.\n464\t   - Vertex foam near shores and sluices.\n465\t   - Anything that falls below the water height spawns a splash.\n466\t6. **Actors as billboards.** Sort far to near; for each actor:\n467\t   - project the foot point; `k = F/z`; skip it if it is under 3 px tall or off screen.\n468\t   - Choose the view with `new E.View('r3', 'Rail3D', yawDeg, pitchDeg, k, 1)`. Take `yawDeg` from the\n469\t     **camera→actor bearing** `b`: `−b·180/π − 90`, as `E.Mode7.view` does from the heading. Take `pitchDeg` from the\n470\t     ray's downward elevation, **clamped to at least 3°** (a View at 1° or less becomes a side view, and Views can't\n471\t     look up). Cache the views by quantized key: yaw and pitch in 2° steps, k in 1/16 steps.\n472\t   - Clear a scratch canvas sized to the actor's bounds × k plus a margin (the engine draws actors up to about\n473\t     250 px), then `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`; the patched engine draws the weapons.\n474\t   - `getImageData`, then for each pixel with alpha ≥ 128: depth = the view z of the actor's chest point − 4 u. If the\n475\t     depth test passes, write `color × actorLight` (mixed 60% toward white while the hit flash is on), and write the\n476\t     depth.\n477\t   - `actorLight = clamp(ambient + sun + Σ lights at the chest, 0.45, 1.25)`, tinted 25% toward the strongest light's\n478\t     color, so actors stay readable at night.\n479\t   - Draw a blob shadow before the actors: a dithered dark ellipse, 7 u in radius, on the ground under each.\n480\t7. **Splats and lines.**\n481\t   - Particles are projected points with a world-unit size. They are depth-tested, never write depth, and are either\n482\t     additive (sparks, fire, muzzle, glows) or dithered alpha (smoke, dust, spray).\n483\t   - Debris uses opaque pixels or `E.sprite` sprites.\n484\t   - Lines (tracers, laser sights, ropes, the lighthouse beam's edges) are depth-tested at their interpolated depth.\n485\t8. **Decals**: bullet holes and scorch marks on colliders' faces, with a depth bias of −0.5 u. A ring buffer holds 160.\n486\t9. **Canvas textures**:\n487\t   - signs, posters, and the festival's giant screens showing Krake's live broadcast, which is `rig.drawPortrait` into\n488\t     a 64×48 canvas, re-read every 4 frames;\n489\t   - consoles' screens;\n490\t   - text painted with `E.font`.\n491\t10. **Present**: `putImageData` into the buffer at the viewport's offset. Mirror `E.Mode7.draw`'s handling of\n492\t    `r.viewport`: `r.viewport || { x: 0, y: 0, w: r.bw, h: r.bh }`.\n493\t11. **Dev overlays** draw after `present`, in screen space: collider wireframes, hit volumes, cover points, rail paths,\n494\t    spawn markers, light radii, AI labels.\n495\t\n496\tCanvas work happens only in `draw`; headless, `draw` is skipped. Create scratch canvases lazily, the first time they\n497\tare drawn, so Node never needs a canvas.\n498\t\n499\t### 4.2 Camera, rail and cover\n500\t- **Logical pose**: the rail plus the slot plus the cover blend. It is deterministic and is the origin of every hitscan\n501\t  ray.\n502\t- **Presentation offsets**, visual only: trauma shake, weapon recoil, travel bob, carrier sway, hit jolt, breathing.\n503\t  They never move the aim ray. The reticle is drawn in screen space, so aiming stays exact.\n504\t- **Cover blend `c`** (0 out, 1 in):\n505\t  - it moves toward its target at `1/coverIn` (0.12 s) or `1/coverOut` (0.15 s);\n506\t  - **exposed means `c < 0.5`**;\n507\t  - pose: `pos = lerp(stand, cover, smooth(c))`, with yaw and pitch on the short way round; `roll = sin(πc)·2°`.\n508\t  - A cover pose sits 10–14 u lower and 6–16 u to the side, and is turned 8–20° away. The cover object fills 40–60% of\n509\t    the screen, so ducking reads instantly.\n510\t- **Arrival**:\n511\t  - each scene has an `arrive` path (`E.Path`, catmull) walked at its speed, easing in and out at the ends;\n512\t  - the look direction follows `look` keys along the path (`'path'` heading, or a world point), slerped;\n513\t  - at the end the camera blends into the slot's stand pose over 0.3 s, then \"ACTION!\" shows and TIME starts.\n514\t  - On foot (speed > 80 u/s): 2 Hz bob, 1.2 u.\n515\t- **Moving scenes**: slots ride a **carrier** (the boat, the funicular car, the tower lift) on its own path. The cover\n516\t  prop is part of the carrier, and waves trigger by the carrier's distance `d`. If enemies are still alive at the end\n517\t  of the path, the carrier stops until they're dead.\n518\t- **Shake**: trauma in 0..1, decaying 1.6/s; the offset is `noise(t·18) · trauma² · 2.5°`, scaled by `settings.shake`,\n519\t  and zero under reduce motion.\n520\t- **Recoil**: pitch kick per shot (handgun 0.6°, MG 0.25° each, shotgun 2.2°, GL 1.5°), with spring recovery.\n521\t- **Hit jolt**: roll 4°, pitch −2°, as a damped spring.\n522\t- **Carrier sway**: boats roll and pitch on slow noise of ±1.5°; the funicular swings ±1°.\n523\t- **Cutscene camera**: keys `[{ t, at, look, fov }]` with easing, plus 16-px letterbox bars. A cutscene can borrow the\n524\t  rail.\n525\t- **Free camera (dev)**:\n526\t  - fly with WASD or the left stick; look with the mouse or the right stick; Q/E or L1/R1 move down/up; Shift goes fast;\n527\t  - **Copy pose** writes `[x, y, z, yaw°, pitch°]` to the clipboard and the console for authoring.\n528\t\n529\t### 4.3 Controls, aiming and prompts\n530\t| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard + mouse | Keyboard only |\n531\t|---|---|---|---|\n532\t| Aim | Right stick (the left stick also aims) | Mouse (absolute reticle, like a light gun) | Arrows / WASD move the reticle |\n533\t| Fire | **R2** (Pad7), also ✕ (Pad0) | **Left click** | Z or J |\n534\t| Take cover (hold; toggle is a setting) | **L2** (Pad6), also ○ (Pad1) | **Right click** or **Space** | X or Shift |\n535\t| Next / previous weapon | R1 / L1 (Pad5/Pad4) | **Wheel**, E / Q | E / Q |\n536\t| Pick a weapon | — | 1 2 3 4 | 1 2 3 4 |\n537\t| Switch while hidden | Fire while in cover cycles to the next weapon with ammo | same | same |\n538\t| Quick reload (ducks for the reload time) | □ (Pad2) | R | R |\n539\t| Pause | Options (Pad9) | Esc / P | Esc / P |\n540\t| Cutscene: next line / skip (hold 0.6 s) | ✕ / hold ✕ | Click or Enter / hold Enter | Enter |\n541\t| Menus | D-pad or stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | Hover focuses, click picks, wheel scrolls; Enter / Esc | Arrows, Enter, Esc |\n542\t\n543\tCreate (Pad8) is never bound: the AI Hub reserves Create+Options. In play, the d-pad nudges the pad reticle.\n544\t\n545\t**The aim model**, per player, in view units. The Sim receives only `aim` (exact, resolution-free).\n546\t- **Mouse.** `aim` comes from `input.pointer()`, mapped through that player's viewport rect, so it sits exactly under\n547\t  the pointer. Hide the OS cursor over the canvas while play is active and the last device is the mouse. When the\n548\t  pointer leaves the canvas, keep the last aim.\n549\t- **Pad.**\n550\t  - Response curve `v = sign(s)·|s|^2.2`; speed 1.6 vu/s × `padSpeed`.\n551\t  - Acceleration up to ×1.5 after the stick has been held 0.35 s.\n552\t  - **Aim assist** (Off, Low .35, Medium .6, High .85; Medium by default):\n553\t    - friction: speed × (1 − 0.55·assist) while the reticle is within 0.07 vu of a target's projected volume;\n554\t    - magnetism: `aim += (center − aim) · min(1, assist·6·dt)`, only while the stick moves (|s| > .2) and the target\n555\t      is within 0.12 vu;\n556\t    - targets are enemies, shootable projectiles, life rings and bottles; never civilians.\n557\t- **Keys.** A constant 1.2 vu/s.\n558\t- In cover the reticle hides. When you pop out, the pad keeps its position; the mouse follows the pointer.\n559\t- **Prompts** always come from `input.label(action)`: `game.input` for P1, `game.players[i]` for the others. They show\n560\t  in a rounded button frame and follow `input.lastDevice` (keyboard/mouse labels like \"Right click\"; the pad's glyph\n561\t  family from the Button symbols setting). Before any input, show both the pad and the keyboard/mouse prompts.\n562\t  Hardcoding a key name anywhere is a bug, and a test greps the source for it.\n563\t\n564\t### 4.4 Weapons\n565\t| | Handgun **\"P9 Marlin\"** | Machine gun **\"Riptide\"** | Shotgun **\"Breakwater\"** | Grenade launcher **\"Squall\"** |\n566\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n567\t| Ammo | 9-round magazine, unlimited reserve | pool, max 240, +60 a pickup | pool, max 36, +8 | pool, max 6, +2 |\n568\t| Fire | semi-auto, up to 6/s; holding auto-repeats at 3.5/s (Auto-fire setting) | full auto, 12/s held | pump, 1.5/s | 1/s |\n569\t| Damage | 1.0 | 0.45 | 8 pellets × 0.45 | 6 at the center, falling to 1.5 at 48 u |\n570\t| Spread | 0 | 0.6°, blooming to 3° (recovers 6°/s) | 5.5° cone | projectile, 640 u/s, gravity 240 u/s² |\n571\t| Special | reloads in cover in 0.30 s | shreds drones and crowds | staggers; knocks shields aside; knocks rushers back | wrecks vehicles, barricades, armor; splash hurts enemies only |\n572\t| Switch time | 0.20 s | 0.25 s | 0.30 s | 0.35 s |\n573\t\n574\t- Hits: head ×2 (HEADSHOT), torso ×1, legs ×0.75 plus a stagger.\n575\t- Special ammo carries over between scenes and stages within a run. An empty special switches back to the handgun.\n576\t- A weapon appears in the cycle once you have ammo for it.\n577\t- You can't fire while `c > 0.2`.\n578\t- \"RELOAD!\" flashes when the magazine is empty.\n579\t- Weapons are registry entries (`def('weapon', …)`) whose numbers are dev sliders.\n580\t\n581\t### 4.5 Player state, TIME and scoring\n582\t- **Lives:** Easy 7, Normal 5, Hard 3. Extra lives come from 150,000 and 400,000 points, and from the one life ring\n583\t  per stage.\n584\t- **After a hit:** 1.5 s of invulnerability, a red border pulse, the chain resets, a camera jolt, rumble (0.6, 0.25 s),\n585\t  and a voice grunt.\n586\t- **Out of lives:**\n587\t  - one player: the Sim freezes for **CONTINUE? 10…0**. Continuing restores lives, **resets the score to 0** (a\n588\t    continue mark is shown beside it) and restarts the current scene's waves.\n589\t  - co-op: each player counts down alone while the Sim runs.\n590\t  - AI Hub: an automatic return after 6 s with −5,000 points.\n591\t- **TIME:**\n592\t  - each scene has its seconds, × difficulty (Easy ×1.25, Hard ×0.85) × a dev slider. It counts only during ACTION\n593\t    and boss fights.\n594\t  - Killing an elite (Red Tide, a sniper) gives +2 s (\"TIME EXTEND +2\").\n595\t  - At 0: **\"TIDE'S IN!\"**, −1 life (this ignores invulnerability), and TIME refills to 60% (a slider).\n596\t  - On a clear: remaining seconds × 100 points.\n597\t\n598\t**Score**\n599\t\n600\t| Event | Points |\n601\t|---|---|\n602\t| Hit on an enemy | 100 |\n603\t| Kill | by archetype (§5.3) |\n604\t| Headshot | +500 |\n605\t| Quick kill (within 0.7 s of exposure) | +500 |\n606\t| A projectile shot down in the air | +1,000 |\n607\t| A breakable | 50 |\n608\t| A bonus target (bottle, ring) | 2,000 |\n609\t| A civilian or hostage hit | −5,000 and −1 life |\n610\t\n611\t**Chain.** +1 per hit. The multiplier is `1 + floor(chain/5)·0.1`, at most ×2.0. A miss (a shot that touches no enemy\n612\tand no bonus target) or a hit taken resets it.\n613\t\n614\t**Stage ranks**\n615\t\n616\t| Rank | Condition |\n617\t|---|---|\n618\t| S | accuracy ≥ 75% and no lives lost |\n619\t| A | accuracy ≥ 60% and ≤ 1 life lost |\n620\t| B | ≥ 45% |\n621\t| C | otherwise |\n622\t| D | a continue was used |\n623\t\n624\t**Stats:** shots, hits, accuracy, headshots, kills, quick kills, cover saves (threats blocked), lives lost, civilians\n625\thit, the best chain, time. They feed the results screen and the AI Hub stats.\n626\t\n627\t### 4.6 Enemies (framework; the roster is in §5.3)\n628\t**Cover points** in the scene data: `{ id, at: [x, y, z], face (yaw toward the players), h: 14 | 40, peek: ['up', 'left', 'right', 'over'], ledge: bool, water: bool }`.\n629\t\n630\t**The state machine**, with timings from the archetype and `sim.rng`:\n631\t```\n632\tSPAWN → ENTER(entry) → HIDE ⇄ PEEK → AIM (maybe a telegraph) → FIRE → HIDE …\n633\t                         ├→ RELOCATE (after n cycles, along a route to another cover point)\n634\t                         ├→ FLEE (quartermaster) / ADVANCE (rusher, shield)\n635\tany → HIT (react) → DEAD (death style) → CORPSE 2.5 s → dithered fade 0.5 s\n636\t```\n637\t**Entries**, each its own animation:\n638\t- `stand`: already there; pops up;\n639\t- `run`: along a route to the cover point;\n640\t- `jump`: down from a roof or container, with an arc, `air` and a heavy `land`;\n641\t- `rappel`: down a rope line, with `climb`, hand over hand;\n642\t- `door`: the door swings open, then the enemy runs out;\n643\t- `vault`: over a barrier;\n644\t- `roll`: a dive into cover (`flip`);\n645\t- `vehicle`: off a boat, jet ski or truck.\n646\t\n647\t**Peeks**:\n648\t- `up`: crouch → stand with `point: true` and `aim` toward the target camera;\n649\t- `left` / `right`: a 10-u side step with a 12° lean;\n650\t- `over`: a shield trooper fires over his shield.\n651\t\n652\tLeaning is done by turning the upper joints about the hips after `rig.update` (the Emberdeep technique: wrap\n653\t`solvePose`).\n654\t\n655\t**Fire plan.** On each exposure: aim for 0.35–0.6 s, then a burst of N shots. Each shot asks the ThreatDirector for\n656\t`threat` or `miss` (§4.7).\n657\t\n658\t**Hit volumes**, rebuilt from the rig's joints every step through `rig.worldOffset(J.*)`. `rig.update` runs headless,\n659\tso they are deterministic.\n660\t- head: a sphere of `headR·size·1.15` at `J.head`;\n661\t- torso: a capsule from the hip center to the neck, radius `torsoW·0.6·size`;\n662\t- legs: a capsule from the hips to the feet, radius 2.2·size;\n663\t- a shield: an oriented box in front of the left forearm, which blocks rays and sparks.\n664\t\n665\tA shot hits the nearest of (volumes ∪ colliders ∪ shootables ∪ civilians) along its ray.\n666\t\n667\t**Reactions**:\n668\t- a 0.06-s white flash; a flinch (`hurt` for 0.25 s);\n669\t- a stagger for leg hits or shotgun hits: knockback 30–60 u/s and a lean back;\n670\t- a headshot snaps the head back 25° (a joint post-process) and the body collapses.\n671\t\n672\t**Death styles**:\n673\t- `crumple`: the engine's `die` pose;\n674\t- `flyback`: a close shotgun blast or an explosion; velocity away from the blast, a roll (`flip`), then `down`;\n675\t- `fall`: off a ledge, with `air`, then lying down;\n676\t- `splash`: into the water, with spray, sinking;\n677\t- `spin`: an MG kill; a 120° turn into `die`.\n678\t\n679\t### 4.7 The ThreatDirector (the crisis flash)\n680\t- **The decision.** A shot becomes a threat if all of these hold:\n681\t  - `rng < chance × tune.threatMul × difficulty`;\n682\t  - the target has fewer active threats than `maxThreats` (Stage 1: 1, Stages 2–3: 2; Easy −1, Hard +1, minimum 1);\n683\t  - `minGap` (0.35 s) has passed since the target's last impact.\n684\t\n685\t  Otherwise it is a miss. Red Tide shots, snipers, rockets, rusher slashes, torpedoes and boss attacks are always\n686\t  threats, but they hold their aim longer to respect `minGap`. **No two impacts on one player land closer together\n687\t  than `minGap`.**\n688\t- **The telegraph**:\n689\t  - a ring at the muzzle's screen point, shrinking from 26 px to 6 px over the telegraph time, red with a white core\n690\t    and a \"!\" glyph (a \"Large\" setting doubles its size);\n691\t  - a muzzle flare and a dynamic light;\n692\t  - a tick at 66% and a sharp chirp at impact;\n693\t  - an edge arrow when the shooter is off screen;\n694\t  - threats aimed at teammates show only a small outline.\n695\t- **Pop-out protection.** If a player leaves cover with less than 0.15 s of a telegraph left, the impact slides 0.15 s\n696\t  later.\n697\t- **Resolution at impact time T**:\n698\t  - exposed, not invulnerable, not in god mode → **HIT** (§4.5);\n699\t  - otherwise **BLOCKED**: the bullet strikes the cover prop (sparks or splinters, a ricochet \"ping\") and the \"cover\n700\t    saves\" stat goes up.\n701\t  - Online, the host resolves at T + 0.2 s, using the cover timeline the client reported (§4.19).\n702\t- **Misses**:\n703\t  - a tracer from the muzzle to a point 8–30 u off the camera, never through the reticle;\n704\t  - a whizz panned by screen x;\n705\t  - an impact effect on the nearest collider behind: metal sparks, wood splinters, concrete dust, water spray, glass.\n706\t\n707\t### 4.8 Projectiles, objects, pickups, civilians and allies\n708\t**Projectiles**: `{ kind, pos, vel, gravity, hp, r (shootable radius), team, target }`. Every one is shootable and\n709\tshows a shrinking ring while it is a threat.\n710\t- **Enemy grenade**: lobbed to land 30–60 u in front of the target's cover in 1.1–1.4 s; hp 1. It is a threat at\n711\t  landing. Shot down in the air, it explodes there, hurting enemies within 48 u, for +1,000.\n712\t- **Rocket**: 220 u/s with a smoke trail; hp 1; a threat on arrival; shot down for +1,000.\n713\t- **Harpoon** (Barracuda): 300 u/s with a rope line; hp 2.\n714\t- **Torpedo**: runs on the surface at 120 u/s with a wake; hp 2. **Cover does not stop it: you have to shoot it.** A\n715\t  big prompt says \"SHOOT THE TORPEDO!\".\n716\t- **Missile** (Scylla): an arc; hp 1.\n717\t- **Flare** (Krake): 160 u/s and glowing; hp 1; it bursts into firework sparks.\n718\t- **Player GL round**: explodes on contact with a collider, an actor or water, or after 1.2 s.\n719\t\n720\t**Breakables** `{ hp, debris, onBreak }`:\n721\t\n722\t| Breakable | hp | Notes |\n723\t|---|---|---|\n724\t| Wooden crate | 3 | Breaking it removes its collider, which can expose an enemy |\n725\t| Window | 1 | Glass |\n726\t| Paper lantern | 1 | Falls and burns for 2 s |\n727\t| Bottles and market goods | 1 | Cosmetic, 50 points |\n728\t| Sign | 2 | Swings |\n729\t| Gallery and barricade sections | scripted | |\n730\t\n731\t**Explosive barrels and tanks**: hp 2, radius 56 u, damage 8. Neighbors chain-explode after 0.15 s. They leave scorch\n732\tdecals, a light, shake and debris.\n733\t\n734\t**Pickups**:\n735\t- Quartermaster ammo, granted on the kill with a banner and the icon flying to the weapon panel;\n736\t- the **life ring** (red and white; shoot it): +1 life, \"1UP!\";\n737\t- the **intel bottle** (green glass; shoot it): added to the INTEL list (§4.20).\n738\t\n739\t**Civilians** (festival-goers, dock workers, fishermen in yellow raincoats) and **hostages**:\n740\t- they have hit volumes and stop bullets; hitting one costs −1 life (even through invulnerability) and −5,000;\n741\t- radio: \"Hold your fire!\";\n742\t- civilians run routes and crouch.\n743\t\n744\t**Allies** (single player): Rook and Mari as scripted actors.\n745\t- Shots pass through them, with a \"Hey—watch it!\" bark at most every 5 s.\n746\t- At cues they make scripted kills, shown as a tracer from the ally.\n747\t- In co-op they appear only in cutscenes.\n748\t\n749\t### 4.9 Bosses (framework)\n750\t```js\n751\tdef('boss', 'stingray', { name: 'STINGRAY', title: 'Black Current gunboat', time: 100,\n752\t  body: G => buildStingrayRig(G),                 // a mesh rig: hull and turret parts, posed by code\n753\t  parts: { turretL: { hp: 12, vol: [...], weak: true }, … },\n754\t  bars: [{ label: 'STINGRAY', parts: ['turretL', 'turretR'] }, { label: 'BARRACUDA', actor: 'barracuda' }],\n755\t  script: function* (B, sim) { /* phases: yields of seconds, predicates, sub-patterns */ } });\n756\t```\n757\t- **Parts** are named hit volumes on a mesh rig's transforms or on a Humanoid's joints. Each has hp and optional armor.\n758\t  A `weak` part pulses gold while it can be damaged, and breaking a part plays its own effects.\n759\t- **HP bars** sit under TIME, with a label and a segment per part. They flash on damage.\n760\t- **Intro**: a 2.5-s name card (\"BARRACUDA — Captain of the Black Current\"), a close-up, a music sting. In AI Hub\n761\t  sessions only the card shows; the camera isn't taken away.\n762\t- Every attack goes through the ThreatDirector and the projectile system, so cover, telegraphs and the tests all work\n763\t  the same for bosses.\n764\t- **Defeat**: 0.6 s of slow motion (`timeScale` 0.35, presentation-side), chained explosions, the death animation,\n765\t  then the outro.\n766\t\n767\t### 4.10 Stage format, the Director and the validators\n768\t```js\n769\tdef('stage', 1, { name: 'HARBOR LIGHTS', place: 'Port Lumen Docks', clock: '23:40', music: 'harbor',\n770\t  env: { sky: 'festival', fog: ['#1a2242', 400, 2000], ambient: .38,\n771\t         sun: { dir: [-.35, .45, .82], color: '#a8b8ff', k: .45 }, water: { z: -24, mat: 'sea-night' },\n772\t         weather: null, fireworks: true },\n773\t  build(G) { /* geometry: brushes and prefabs (§5.10) */ },\n774\t  intro: 'c1-intro', outro: 'c1-outro', scenes: ['1-1', '1-2', '1-3', '1-4', '1-B'] });\n775\t\n776\tdef('scene', '1-1', { title: 'LANTERN PIER', time: 45,\n777\t  arrive: { path: [[-160, 0, 24], [-60, -10, 24], [0, -20, 24]], speed: 110,\n778\t            look: [[0, 'path'], [.8, [300, 0, 18]]] },\n779\t  slots: [   // P1 on the left, P2 on the right (facing east, +y is to the right)\n780\t    { stand: { at: [0, -20, 24], look: [300, -10, 16] }, cover: { at: [-6, -32, 12], look: [300, -60, 10] } },\n781\t    { stand: { at: [0, 22, 24], look: [300, 10, 16] },   cover: { at: [-6, 34, 12], look: [300, 60, 10] } } ],\n782\t  covers: { c1: { at: [160, -30, 0], h: 16, peek: ['up'] },\n783\t            c2: { at: [180, 30, 0], h: 16, peek: ['up', 'right'] }, … },\n784\t  waves: [\n785\t    { at: .5, spawn: [['deckhand', 'c1', { entry: 'stand' }], ['deckhand', 'c2'], ['deckhand', 'c3']] },\n786\t    { after: 'clear', spawn: [['deckhand', 'c5', { entry: 'door' }], ['deckhand', 'c4', { entry: 'jump' }]] },\n787\t    { after: 'clear', spawn: [['quartermaster', null, { route: [[360, -80, 0], [360, 90, 0]], drop: 'mg', flee: 3.5 }],\n788\t                              ['deckhand', 'c6', { entry: 'run', from: [420, -60, 0] }]] } ],\n789\t  civilians: [{ at: 2, kind: 'festival-pair', route: [[120, -50, 0], [300, -50, 0]] }],\n790\t  objects: [['lifering', [100, 58, 18]], ['lanterns', 'stalls'], ['bottles', 'c1']],\n791\t  cues: [{ at: 0, say: ['juno', 'Hostiles on the pier! Watch the festival crowd!'] },\n792\t         { on: 'spawn:quartermaster', say: ['juno', \"Orange vest! He's hauling ammo—drop him!\"] }] });\n793\t```\n794\t- **Director phases**: `intro` (cutscene) → `travel` (WAIT) → `action` → `clear` (the time bonus counts up, 1.2 s)\n795\t  → `travel` … → `boss` → `outro` → results.\n796\t- A wave starts by `at` (seconds into the action), `atD` (carrier distance), `after: 'clear' | '<waveId>' | 'kills:N'`,\n797\t  or `on: '<event>'`.\n798\t- A scene clears when every non-civilian it spawned is dead and no wave is pending.\n799\t- Cues: `say` (radio, not modal), `cut` (a short modal line), `prompt` (a tutorial hint, the first time only), `fx`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"f6aafc7e-3f91-4a8f-961d-0dd8c7cbcd87","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:33.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 4.1 Rail3D, the renderer\n**Data**\n- **Mesh**: `{ groups: [{ mat, pos: Float32Array, nrm, uv, lit: Float32Array (baked light per vertex), flags }], bounds, sphere }`.\n- **TextureBank** (built at boot):\n  - each material has 5 band tiles: `E.materialTile(id, { size: 32, px: 2, band: 0..4 })`, plus `lid: true` versions\n    for faces that look up or down. Each tile is converted to a `Uint32Array`.\n  - Tiles are `v`-up with the top row first, so flip v when sampling.\n  - Face-pattern materials (crate) use uv 0..1 across each face.\n  - Use **named** materials in shape entries so `materialTile(id)` resolves them. Register any inline material in\n    `E.MATERIALS` under a generated id first.\n  - Material flags: `glow` (emissive), `water`, `double` (draw both sides), `alphaTest` (nets, grates, foliage cards,\n    on the tile's alpha or a pattern mask), `scroll` (uv speed).\n- **Instances**: `{ mesh, M (3×4), visible, dynamic, tint, flash, collider ids }`.\n- **Static world**: built when a stage is built, then transformed to world space and baked. The baked light is\n  `ambient + sunK·max(0, n·sun) + Σ static lights` plus contact darkening where a wall meets the floor. Tessellate\n  faces to edges of 64 u or less so the vertex light, fog and near clipping stay clean. Bin it into 256-u chunks with\n  bounding spheres for frustum culling.\n\n**Per viewport, per frame**\n1. `begin(cam, rect)`: the basis, `F`, the frustum planes; clear the depth to `+∞`.\n2. **Sky**, per pixel from the ray's elevation e and azimuth a:\n   - a three-stop gradient (the stage palette);\n   - stars from a hash of the quantized direction where e > 0.05, twinkling;\n   - a moon or sun disc with a halo;\n   - two octaves of drifting noise clouds;\n   - one to three distant silhouette layers on the horizon (`h(a)` heightfields: skyline, cliffs, the barrier);\n   - lightning brightens it.\n3. **Triangles**, for each visible group:\n   - transform to view space, clip against the near plane (z = 2 u; Sutherland–Hodgman, a triangle becomes 0–2),\n     project, and cull back faces unless the material is `double`;\n   - rasterize over the integer bounding box with edge functions and a top-left fill rule. Interpolate `1/z`, `u/z`,\n     `v/z` and `L/z` for perspective-correct values;\n   - depth test on view z;\n   - per pixel: `band = clamp(floor(L·4 + bayer4[x&3][y&3]), 0, 4)` (the engine's banded light, dithered between\n     bands) → texel → fog → write color and depth;\n   - fog `f = clamp((z − near)/(far − near))^1.2`, quantized to 8 steps with the Bayer threshold. Emissive materials\n     skip lighting and take half the fog.\n   - *Retro wobble* (a setting, off by default) snaps vertices to whole pixels and makes texturing affine.\n4. **Dynamic light** on top of the baked light: up to 12 point lights per frame (muzzle flashes, explosions, flares,\n   the lighthouse beam, the tram's lamps). Each adds `k·(1 − d/r)²` per vertex, only for triangles whose bounding\n   sphere it touches.\n5. **Water**: a material with `water: true`.\n   - The band comes from `base + 0.6·sin(u·.11 + t·1.3)·sin(v·.07 − t)` plus noise.\n   - Sparkles: the `hi` color where noise(u + t·8, v) > 0.82, weighted toward the moon or sun direction.\n   - Vertex foam near shores and sluices.\n   - Anything that falls below the water height spawns a splash.\n6. **Actors as billboards.** Sort far to near; for each actor:\n   - project the foot point; `k = F/z`; skip it if it is under 3 px tall or off screen.\n   - Choose the view with `new E.View('r3', 'Rail3D', yawDeg, pitchDeg, k, 1)`. Take `yawDeg` from the\n     **camera→actor bearing** `b`: `−b·180/π − 90`, as `E.Mode7.view` does from the heading. Take `pitchDeg` from the\n     ray's downward elevation, **clamped to at least 3°** (a View at 1° or less becomes a side view, and Views can't\n     look up). Cache the views by quantized key: yaw and pitch in 2° steps, k in 1/16 steps.\n   - Clear a scratch canvas sized to the actor's bounds × k plus a margin (the engine draws actors up to about\n     250 px), then `rig.draw(g, ox, oy, view)`; the patched engine draws the weapons.\n   - `getImageData`, then for each pixel with alpha ≥ 128: depth = the view z of the actor's chest point − 4 u. If the\n     depth test passes, write `color × actorLight` (mixed 60% toward white while the hit flash is on), and write the\n     depth.\n   - `actorLight = clamp(ambient + sun + Σ lights at the chest, 0.45, 1.25)`, tinted 25% toward the strongest light's\n     color, so actors stay readable at night.\n   - Draw a blob shadow before the actors: a dithered dark ellipse, 7 u in radius, on the ground under each.\n7. **Splats and lines.**\n   - Particles are projected points with a world-unit size. They are depth-tested, never write depth, and are either\n     additive (sparks, fire, muzzle, glows) or dithered alpha (smoke, dust, spray).\n   - Debris uses opaque pixels or `E.sprite` sprites.\n   - Lines (tracers, laser sights, ropes, the lighthouse beam's edges) are depth-tested at their interpolated depth.\n8. **Decals**: bullet holes and scorch marks on colliders' faces, with a depth bias of −0.5 u. A ring buffer holds 160.\n9. **Canvas textures**:\n   - signs, posters, and the festival's giant screens showing Krake's live broadcast, which is `rig.drawPortrait` into\n     a 64×48 canvas, re-read every 4 frames;\n   - consoles' screens;\n   - text painted with `E.font`.\n10. **Present**: `putImageData` into the buffer at the viewport's offset. Mirror `E.Mode7.draw`'s handling of\n    `r.viewport`: `r.viewport || { x: 0, y: 0, w: r.bw, h: r.bh }`.\n11. **Dev overlays** draw after `present`, in screen space: collider wireframes, hit volumes, cover points, rail paths,\n    spawn markers, light radii, AI labels.\n\nCanvas work happens only in `draw`; headless, `draw` is skipped. Create scratch canvases lazily, the first time they\nare drawn, so Node never needs a canvas.\n\n### 4.2 Camera, rail and cover\n- **Logical pose**: the rail plus the slot plus the cover blend. It is deterministic and is the origin of every hitscan\n  ray.\n- **Presentation offsets**, visual only: trauma shake, weapon recoil, travel bob, carrier sway, hit jolt, breathing.\n  They never move the aim ray. The reticle is drawn in screen space, so aiming stays exact.\n- **Cover blend `c`** (0 out, 1 in):\n  - it moves toward its target at `1/coverIn` (0.12 s) or `1/coverOut` (0.15 s);\n  - **exposed means `c < 0.5`**;\n  - pose: `pos = lerp(stand, cover, smooth(c))`, with yaw and pitch on the short way round; `roll = sin(πc)·2°`.\n  - A cover pose sits 10–14 u lower and 6–16 u to the side, and is turned 8–20° away. The cover object fills 40–60% of\n    the screen, so ducking reads instantly.\n- **Arrival**:\n  - each scene has an `arrive` path (`E.Path`, catmull) walked at its speed, easing in and out at the ends;\n  - the look direction follows `look` keys along the path (`'path'` heading, or a world point), slerped;\n  - at the end the camera blends into the slot's stand pose over 0.3 s, then \"ACTION!\" shows and TIME starts.\n  - On foot (speed > 80 u/s): 2 Hz bob, 1.2 u.\n- **Moving scenes**: slots ride a **carrier** (the boat, the funicular car, the tower lift) on its own path. The cover\n  prop is part of the carrier, and waves trigger by the carrier's distance `d`. If enemies are still alive at the end\n  of the path, the carrier stops until they're dead.\n- **Shake**: trauma in 0..1, decaying 1.6/s; the offset is `noise(t·18) · trauma² · 2.5°`, scaled by `settings.shake`,\n  and zero under reduce motion.\n- **Recoil**: pitch kick per shot (handgun 0.6°, MG 0.25° each, shotgun 2.2°, GL 1.5°), with spring recovery.\n- **Hit jolt**: roll 4°, pitch −2°, as a damped spring.\n- **Carrier sway**: boats roll and pitch on slow noise of ±1.5°; the funicular swings ±1°.\n- **Cutscene camera**: keys `[{ t, at, look, fov }]` with easing, plus 16-px letterbox bars. A cutscene can borrow the\n  rail.\n- **Free camera (dev)**:\n  - fly with WASD or the left stick; look with the mouse or the right stick; Q/E or L1/R1 move down/up; Shift goes fast;\n  - **Copy pose** writes `[x, y, z, yaw°, pitch°]` to the clipboard and the console for authoring.\n\n### 4.3 Controls, aiming and prompts\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard + mouse | Keyboard only |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Aim | Right stick (the left stick also aims) | Mouse (absolute reticle, like a light gun) | Arrows / WASD move the reticle |\n| Fire | **R2** (Pad7), also ✕ (Pad0) | **Left click** | Z or J |\n| Take cover (hold; toggle is a setting) | **L2** (Pad6), also ○ (Pad1) | **Right click** or **Space** | X or Shift |\n| Next / previous weapon | R1 / L1 (Pad5/Pad4) | **Wheel**, E / Q | E / Q |\n| Pick a weapon | — | 1 2 3 4 | 1 2 3 4 |\n| Switch while hidden | Fire while in cover cycles to the next weapon with ammo | same | same |\n| Quick reload (ducks for the reload time) | □ (Pad2) | R | R |\n| Pause | Options (Pad9) | Esc / P | Esc / P |\n| Cutscene: next line / skip (hold 0.6 s) | ✕ / hold ✕ | Click or Enter / hold Enter | Enter |\n| Menus | D-pad or stick, ✕ confirm, ○ back | Hover focuses, click picks, wheel scrolls; Enter / Esc | Arrows, Enter, Esc |\n\nCreate (Pad8) is never bound: the AI Hub reserves Create+Options. In play, the d-pad nudges the pad reticle.\n\n**The aim model**, per player, in view units. The Sim receives only `aim` (exact, resolution-free).\n- **Mouse.** `aim` comes from `input.pointer()`, mapped through that player's viewport rect, so it sits exactly under\n  the pointer. Hide the OS cursor over the canvas while play is active and the last device is the mouse. When the\n  pointer leaves the canvas, keep the last aim.\n- **Pad.**\n  - Response curve `v = sign(s)·|s|^2.2`; speed 1.6 vu/s × `padSpeed`.\n  - Acceleration up to ×1.5 after the stick has been held 0.35 s.\n  - **Aim assist** (Off, Low .35, Medium .6, High .85; Medium by default):\n    - friction: speed × (1 − 0.55·assist) while the reticle is within 0.07 vu of a target's projected volume;\n    - magnetism: `aim += (center − aim) · min(1, assist·6·dt)`, only while the stick moves (|s| > .2) and the target\n      is within 0.12 vu;\n    - targets are enemies, shootable projectiles, life rings and bottles; never civilians.\n- **Keys.** A constant 1.2 vu/s.\n- In cover the reticle hides. When you pop out, the pad keeps its position; the mouse follows the pointer.\n- **Prompts** always come from `input.label(action)`: `game.input` for P1, `game.players[i]` for the others. They show\n  in a rounded button frame and follow `input.lastDevice` (keyboard/mouse labels like \"Right click\"; the pad's glyph\n  family from the Button symbols setting). Before any input, show both the pad and the keyboard/mouse prompts.\n  Hardcoding a key name anywhere is a bug, and a test greps the source for it.\n\n### 4.4 Weapons\n| | Handgun **\"P9 Marlin\"** | Machine gun **\"Riptide\"** | Shotgun **\"Breakwater\"** | Grenade launcher **\"Squall\"** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Ammo | 9-round magazine, unlimited reserve | pool, max 240, +60 a pickup | pool, max 36, +8 | pool, max 6, +2 |\n| Fire | semi-auto, up to 6/s; holding auto-repeats at 3.5/s (Auto-fire setting) | full auto, 12/s held | pump, 1.5/s | 1/s |\n| Damage | 1.0 | 0.45 | 8 pellets × 0.45 | 6 at the center, falling to 1.5 at 48 u |\n| Spread | 0 | 0.6°, blooming to 3° (recovers 6°/s) | 5.5° cone | projectile, 640 u/s, gravity 240 u/s² |\n| Special | reloads in cover in 0.30 s | shreds drones and crowds | staggers; knocks shields aside; knocks rushers back | wrecks vehicles, barricades, armor; splash hurts enemies only |\n| Switch time | 0.20 s | 0.25 s | 0.30 s | 0.35 s |\n\n- Hits: head ×2 (HEADSHOT), torso ×1, legs ×0.75 plus a stagger.\n- Special ammo carries over between scenes and stages within a run. An empty special switches back to the handgun.\n- A weapon appears in the cycle once you have ammo for it.\n- You can't fire while `c > 0.2`.\n- \"RELOAD!\" flashes when the magazine is empty.\n- Weapons are registry entries (`def('weapon', …)`) whose numbers are dev sliders.\n\n### 4.5 Player state, TIME and scoring\n- **Lives:** Easy 7, Normal 5, Hard 3. Extra lives come from 150,000 and 400,000 points, and from the one life ring\n  per stage.\n- **After a hit:** 1.5 s of invulnerability, a red border pulse, the chain resets, a camera jolt, rumble (0.6, 0.25 s),\n  and a voice grunt.\n- **Out of lives:**\n  - one player: the Sim freezes for **CONTINUE? 10…0**. Continuing restores lives, **resets the score to 0** (a\n    continue mark is shown beside it) and restarts the current scene's waves.\n  - co-op: each player counts down alone while the Sim runs.\n  - AI Hub: an automatic return after 6 s with −5,000 points.\n- **TIME:**\n  - each scene has its seconds, × difficulty (Easy ×1.25, Hard ×0.85) × a dev slider. It counts only during ACTION\n    and boss fights.\n  - Killing an elite (Red Tide, a sniper) gives +2 s (\"TIME EXTEND +2\").\n  - At 0: **\"TIDE'S IN!\"**, −1 life (this ignores invulnerability), and TIME refills to 60% (a slider).\n  - On a clear: remaining seconds × 100 points.\n\n**Score**\n\n| Event | Points |\n|---|---|\n| Hit on an enemy | 100 |\n| Kill | by archetype (§5.3) |\n| Headshot | +500 |\n| Quick kill (within 0.7 s of exposure) | +500 |\n| A projectile shot down in the air | +1,000 |\n| A breakable | 50 |\n| A bonus target (bottle, ring) | 2,000 |\n| A civilian or hostage hit | −5,000 and −1 life |\n\n**Chain.** +1 per hit. The multiplier is `1 + floor(chain/5)·0.1`, at most ×2.0. A miss (a shot that touches no enemy\nand no bonus target) or a hit taken resets it.\n\n**Stage ranks**\n\n| Rank | Condition |\n|---|---|\n| S | accuracy ≥ 75% and no lives lost |\n| A | accuracy ≥ 60% and ≤ 1 life lost |\n| B | ≥ 45% |\n| C | otherwise |\n| D | a continue was used |\n\n**Stats:** shots, hits, accuracy, headshots, kills, quick kills, cover saves (threats blocked), lives lost, civilians\nhit, the best chain, time. They feed the results screen and the AI Hub stats.\n\n### 4.6 Enemies (framework; the roster is in §5.3)\n**Cover points** in the scene data: `{ id, at: [x, y, z], face (yaw toward the players), h: 14 | 40, peek: ['up', 'left', 'right', 'over'], ledge: bool, water: bool }`.\n\n**The state machine**, with timings from the archetype and `sim.rng`:\n```\nSPAWN → ENTER(entry) → HIDE ⇄ PEEK → AIM (maybe a telegraph) → FIRE → HIDE …\n                         ├→ RELOCATE (after n cycles, along a route to another cover point)\n                         ├→ FLEE (quartermaster) / ADVANCE (rusher, shield)\nany → HIT (react) → DEAD (death style) → CORPSE 2.5 s → dithered fade 0.5 s\n```\n**Entries**, each its own animation:\n- `stand`: already there; pops up;\n- `run`: along a route to the cover point;\n- `jump`: down from a roof or container, with an arc, `air` and a heavy `land`;\n- `rappel`: down a rope line, with `climb`, hand over hand;\n- `door`: the door swings open, then the enemy runs out;\n- `vault`: over a barrier;\n- `roll`: a dive into cover (`flip`);\n- `vehicle`: off a boat, jet ski or truck.\n\n**Peeks**:\n- `up`: crouch → stand with `point: true` and `aim` toward the target camera;\n- `left` / `right`: a 10-u side step with a 12° lean;\n- `over`: a shield trooper fires over his shield.\n\nLeaning is done by turning the upper joints about the hips after `rig.update` (the Emberdeep technique: wrap\n`solvePose`).\n\n**Fire plan.** On each exposure: aim for 0.35–0.6 s, then a burst of N shots. Each shot asks the ThreatDirector for\n`threat` or `miss` (§4.7).\n\n**Hit volumes**, rebuilt from the rig's joints every step through `rig.worldOffset(J.*)`. `rig.update` runs headless,\nso they are deterministic.\n- head: a sphere of `headR·size·1.15` at `J.head`;\n- torso: a capsule from the hip center to the neck, radius `torsoW·0.6·size`;\n- legs: a capsule from the hips to the feet, radius 2.2·size;\n- a shield: an oriented box in front of the left forearm, which blocks rays and sparks.\n\nA shot hits the nearest of (volumes ∪ colliders ∪ shootables ∪ civilians) along its ray.\n\n**Reactions**:\n- a 0.06-s white flash; a flinch (`hurt` for 0.25 s);\n- a stagger for leg hits or shotgun hits: knockback 30–60 u/s and a lean back;\n- a headshot snaps the head back 25° (a joint post-process) and the body collapses.\n\n**Death styles**:\n- `crumple`: the engine's `die` pose;\n- `flyback`: a close shotgun blast or an explosion; velocity away from the blast, a roll (`flip`), then `down`;\n- `fall`: off a ledge, with `air`, then lying down;\n- `splash`: into the water, with spray, sinking;\n- `spin`: an MG kill; a 120° turn into `die`.\n\n### 4.7 The ThreatDirector (the crisis flash)\n- **The decision.** A shot becomes a threat if all of these hold:\n  - `rng < chance × tune.threatMul × difficulty`;\n  - the target has fewer active threats than `maxThreats` (Stage 1: 1, Stages 2–3: 2; Easy −1, Hard +1, minimum 1);\n  - `minGap` (0.35 s) has passed since the target's last impact.\n\n  Otherwise it is a miss. Red Tide shots, snipers, rockets, rusher slashes, torpedoes and boss attacks are always\n  threats, but they hold their aim longer to respect `minGap`. **No two impacts on one player land closer together\n  than `minGap`.**\n- **The telegraph**:\n  - a ring at the muzzle's screen point, shrinking from 26 px to 6 px over the telegraph time, red with a white core\n    and a \"!\" glyph (a \"Large\" setting doubles its size);\n  - a muzzle flare and a dynamic light;\n  - a tick at 66% and a sharp chirp at impact;\n  - an edge arrow when the shooter is off screen;\n  - threats aimed at teammates show only a small outline.\n- **Pop-out protection.** If a player leaves cover with less than 0.15 s of a telegraph left, the impact slides 0.15 s\n  later.\n- **Resolution at impact time T**:\n  - exposed, not invulnerable, not in god mode → **HIT** (§4.5);\n  - otherwise **BLOCKED**: the bullet strikes the cover prop (sparks or splinters, a ricochet \"ping\") and the \"cover\n    saves\" stat goes up.\n  - Online, the host resolves at T + 0.2 s, using the cover timeline the client reported (§4.19).\n- **Misses**:\n  - a tracer from the muzzle to a point 8–30 u off the camera, never through the reticle;\n  - a whizz panned by screen x;\n  - an impact effect on the nearest collider behind: metal sparks, wood splinters, concrete dust, water spray, glass.\n\n### 4.8 Projectiles, objects, pickups, civilians and allies\n**Projectiles**: `{ kind, pos, vel, gravity, hp, r (shootable radius), team, target }`. Every one is shootable and\nshows a shrinking ring while it is a threat.\n- **Enemy grenade**: lobbed to land 30–60 u in front of the target's cover in 1.1–1.4 s; hp 1. It is a threat at\n  landing. Shot down in the air, it explodes there, hurting enemies within 48 u, for +1,000.\n- **Rocket**: 220 u/s with a smoke trail; hp 1; a threat on arrival; shot down for +1,000.\n- **Harpoon** (Barracuda): 300 u/s with a rope line; hp 2.\n- **Torpedo**: runs on the surface at 120 u/s with a wake; hp 2. **Cover does not stop it: you have to shoot it.** A\n  big prompt says \"SHOOT THE TORPEDO!\".\n- **Missile** (Scylla): an arc; hp 1.\n- **Flare** (Krake): 160 u/s and glowing; hp 1; it bursts into firework sparks.\n- **Player GL round**: explodes on contact with a collider, an actor or water, or after 1.2 s.\n\n**Breakables** `{ hp, debris, onBreak }`:\n\n| Breakable | hp | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Wooden crate | 3 | Breaking it removes its collider, which can expose an enemy |\n| Window | 1 | Glass |\n| Paper lantern | 1 | Falls and burns for 2 s |\n| Bottles and market goods | 1 | Cosmetic, 50 points |\n| Sign | 2 | Swings |\n| Gallery and barricade sections | scripted | |\n\n**Explosive barrels and tanks**: hp 2, radius 56 u, damage 8. Neighbors chain-explode after 0.15 s. They leave scorch\ndecals, a light, shake and debris.\n\n**Pickups**:\n- Quartermaster ammo, granted on the kill with a banner and the icon flying to the weapon panel;\n- the **life ring** (red and white; shoot it): +1 life, \"1UP!\";\n- the **intel bottle** (green glass; shoot it): added to the INTEL list (§4.20).\n\n**Civilians** (festival-goers, dock workers, fishermen in yellow raincoats) and **hostages**:\n- they have hit volumes and stop bullets; hitting one costs −1 life (even through invulnerability) and −5,000;\n- radio: \"Hold your fire!\";\n- civilians run routes and crouch.\n\n**Allies** (single player): Rook and Mari as scripted actors.\n- Shots pass through them, with a \"Hey—watch it!\" bark at most every 5 s.\n- At cues they make scripted kills, shown as a tracer from the ally.\n- In co-op they appear only in cutscenes.\n\n### 4.9 Bosses (framework)\n```js\ndef('boss', 'stingray', { name: 'STINGRAY', title: 'Black Current gunboat', time: 100,\n  body: G => buildStingrayRig(G),                 // a mesh rig: hull and turret parts, posed by code\n  parts: { turretL: { hp: 12, vol: [...], weak: true }, … },\n  bars: [{ label: 'STINGRAY', parts: ['turretL', 'turretR'] }, { label: 'BARRACUDA', actor: 'barracuda' }],\n  script: function* (B, sim) { /* phases: yields of seconds, predicates, sub-patterns */ } });\n```\n- **Parts** are named hit volumes on a mesh rig's transforms or on a Humanoid's joints. Each has hp and optional armor.\n  A `weak` part pulses gold while it can be damaged, and breaking a part plays its own effects.\n- **HP bars** sit under TIME, with a label and a segment per part. They flash on damage.\n- **Intro**: a 2.5-s name card (\"BARRACUDA — Captain of the Black Current\"), a close-up, a music sting. In AI Hub\n  sessions only the card shows; the camera isn't taken away.\n- Every attack goes through the ThreatDirector and the projectile system, so cover, telegraphs and the tests all work\n  the same for bosses.\n- **Defeat**: 0.6 s of slow motion (`timeScale` 0.35, presentation-side), chained explosions, the death animation,\n  then the outro.\n\n### 4.10 Stage format, the Director and the validators\n```js\ndef('stage', 1, { name: 'HARBOR LIGHTS', place: 'Port Lumen Docks', clock: '23:40', music: 'harbor',\n  env: { sky: 'festival', fog: ['#1a2242', 400, 2000], ambient: .38,\n         sun: { dir: [-.35, .45, .82], color: '#a8b8ff', k: .45 }, water: { z: -24, mat: 'sea-night' },\n         weather: null, fireworks: true },\n  build(G) { /* geometry: brushes and prefabs (§5.10) */ },\n  intro: 'c1-intro', outro: 'c1-outro', scenes: ['1-1', '1-2', '1-3', '1-4', '1-B'] });\n\ndef('scene', '1-1', { title: 'LANTERN PIER', time: 45,\n  arrive: { path: [[-160, 0, 24], [-60, -10, 24], [0, -20, 24]], speed: 110,\n            look: [[0, 'path'], [.8, [300, 0, 18]]] },\n  slots: [   // P1 on the left, P2 on the right (facing east, +y is to the right)\n    { stand: { at: [0, -20, 24], look: [300, -10, 16] }, cover: { at: [-6, -32, 12], look: [300, -60, 10] } },\n    { stand: { at: [0, 22, 24], look: [300, 10, 16] },   cover: { at: [-6, 34, 12], look: [300, 60, 10] } } ],\n  covers: { c1: { at: [160, -30, 0], h: 16, peek: ['up'] },\n            c2: { at: [180, 30, 0], h: 16, peek: ['up', 'right'] }, … },\n  waves: [\n    { at: .5, spawn: [['deckhand', 'c1', { entry: 'stand' }], ['deckhand', 'c2'], ['deckhand', 'c3']] },\n    { after: 'clear', spawn: [['deckhand', 'c5', { entry: 'door' }], ['deckhand', 'c4', { entry: 'jump' }]] },\n    { after: 'clear', spawn: [['quartermaster', null, { route: [[360, -80, 0], [360, 90, 0]], drop: 'mg', flee: 3.5 }],\n                              ['deckhand', 'c6', { entry: 'run', from: [420, -60, 0] }]] } ],\n  civilians: [{ at: 2, kind: 'festival-pair', route: [[120, -50, 0], [300, -50, 0]] }],\n  objects: [['lifering', [100, 58, 18]], ['lanterns', 'stalls'], ['bottles', 'c1']],\n  cues: [{ at: 0, say: ['juno', 'Hostiles on the pier! Watch the festival crowd!'] },\n         { on: 'spawn:quartermaster', say: ['juno', \"Orange vest! He's hauling ammo—drop him!\"] }] });\n```\n- **Director phases**: `intro` (cutscene) → `travel` (WAIT) → `action` → `clear` (the time bonus counts up, 1.2 s)\n  → `travel` … → `boss` → `outro` → results.\n- A wave starts by `at` (seconds into the action), `atD` (carrier distance), `after: 'clear' | '<waveId>' | 'kills:N'`,\n  or `on: '<event>'`.\n- A scene clears when every non-civilian it spawned is dead and no wave is pending.\n- Cues: `say` (radio, not modal), `cut` (a short modal line), `prompt` (a tutorial hint, the first time only), `fx`","numLines":380,"startLine":420,"totalLines":1671}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011HotVGUiePKqyEf9cmCwW9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
