{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2fvQdS5U4HZ9d61EjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full plan is far more than one run can finish at its stated fidelity, so I'll scope the build deliberately. Before deciding what to cut, I need the engine's real API for the parts I'll depend on: the Humanoid rig, Mode 7 views, the game loop, menus and audio. I'll look those up in the engine's index."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12605,"cache_read_input_tokens":56109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12605},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"4331d592-9fe2-441b-a187-81054e093548","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:39.679Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2fvBEgtp3oFyyxQYKk"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2fvQdS5U4HZ9d61EjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D6EhXqauZtbbZcYfcbtUET","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/tc3-haiku-20261103/engine/dist/handoff && head -120 API-INDEX.md","description":"Read engine API index header"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12605,"cache_read_input_tokens":56109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12605},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"056bc265-09fc-4678-acc1-2cf9e5b9d33e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:40.028Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2fvBEgtp3oFyyxQYKk","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01D6EhXqauZtbbZcYfcbtUET":{"command":"cd ~/.cache/tc3-haiku-20261103/engine/dist/handoff && head -120 API-INDEX.md","description":"Read engine API index header"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D6EhXqauZtbbZcYfcbtUET","type":"tool_result","content":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\nif (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\nif (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\nconst up = map.ledge(hero, 0);   // east, toward the roof\nif (!up || up.z !== 40) throw new Error('a ledge to climb onto the roof');\n```\n\n## Contents\n\nThe line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n\n- 108 The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n- 119 Math\n- 194 Pixel primitives\n- 213 Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n- 246 Screen; game.screen\n- 268 Input; E.Input: input\n- 353 Pixel font\n- 364 Lighting; game.lights\n- 383 Particles; E.Particles: game.particles\n- 403 Renderer; r\n- 451 Game; E.Game: game\n- 562 Standard features; settings, fullscreen\n- 579 10c. Boot\n- 584 10d. Tweens and scripts; E.Script: script, E.Tween: tween\n- 601 10e. Paths; E.Path: path\n- 611 10g. Weather\n- 615 10k. Save slots; E.Saves: saves\n- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n- 731 Tile map; E.TileMap: map\n- 794 Materials\n- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n- 833 Texture helpers for floortex functions\n- 844 Platform map; E.PlatformMap: level\n- 878 Platformer; E.Platformer: hero\n- 919 Body; E.Body: body\n- 939 Actions; E.Action: action\n- 961 17c. Mover; E.Mover: mover\n- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n- 1017 Bullets; E.Bullets: shots\n- 1037 Spatial hash; E.SpatialHash: grid\n- 1047 Audio; game.audio\n- 1079 Backdrops; E.Backdrop: backdrop\n- 1087 21c. Props\n- 1092 21e. Shapes\n- 1104 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n- 1190 Gpu lighting (webgpu); game.gpu\n- 1211 Sessions\n- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n- 1255 Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js); E.Click: click, E.Walkbox: walkbox\n- 1300 Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js); E.Car: car, E.Race: race\n- 1338 Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js); E.FightAI: fightai, E.FightSelect: fightselect, E.FightStage: fightstage, E.Fighter: fighter, E.Match: match\n- 1419 Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed (engine/modules/gen.js)\n- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n- 1489 Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js); E.Mode7: mode7\n- 1512 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\n- 1541 Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js); E.Rhythm: rhythm\n- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n- 1590 Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js); E.World: world\n- 1619 Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters (engine/modules/rpg.js); E.RPG: rpg\n- 1638 Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\n- 1646 Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js); E.Story: story\n- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n- 1721 Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js); E.Terrain: terrain\n\n## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n\n- `E.DEG: 0.017453292519943295`: π/180, one degree in radians (angle * DEG)\n- `E.TAU: 6.283185307179586`: 2π, a full turn in radians\n- `E.build: \"dev-build\"`: the commit this copy was built from, a placeholder in the repo that tools/stamp.mjs replaces when the site deploys (e.g. 'a1b2c3d 2026-10-07')\n- `E.current: null`: the latest game made (My3D2dge.current, for tools and tests)\n- `E.name: \"my-3D2dge\"`: the engine's name, 'my-3D2dge'\n- `E.version: \"0.85.2\"`: the release (package.json, written everywhere by node tools/version.mjs)\n- `E.versionLabel()`: 'v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': the label to show on screens and in reports\n- `E.warn(key, msg)`: one console warning per distinct problem, prefixed so tools (and people) can spot engine advice: warn(key, message)\n\n## 1. Math\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"4bc96a8d-309c-405f-a376-c419e3941237","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:35:40.045Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# my-3D2dge API index (v0.85.2)\n\nEvery public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n\n## Units and the height rules\n\n| Quantity | Unit |\n| --- | --- |\n| Distances, positions, sizes in the world | world units: one floor tile is 16; x east, y south, z up |\n| Speeds, gravity | world units per second, per second squared |\n| Time, `dt` | seconds (`dt` is one fixed step: 1/120 s of real time times `game.timeScale`) |\n| Angles, `facing`, `dir` | radians: 0 east, π/2 south (a direction may also be a ground vector `[dx, dy]`) |\n| Screen positions | pixels of the game's own low-resolution buffer (`game.screen.W` × `H`) |\n| Colors | `'#rrggbb'` strings |\n\n- A body's `z` is its feet. A cell's top is `map.height(cx, cy)`: 0 on the floor; a wall is solid from 0 up to its `h`.\n- A body stands on the highest top within `z + 2` under its footprint (`E.HEIGHTS.step`, `Body.step`).\n- Eyes are at `z + 30` and a target is seen at `z + 22` (`E.HEIGHTS.eye`, `chest`; a body's own `eye` and `chest` override them).\n- Two things are on the same level when `|dz| <= 8` (`E.HEIGHTS.level`), unless a call says otherwise.\n- Collision, standing, sight (`map.sight`, `map.ray`), reach (`E.targets`, `E.inArc` with `dz`) and navigation (`E.FlowField`) all follow these rules. `E.dist` is 3D; `E.overlap` is flat.\n\n## Examples\n\nEach runs in `tools/contract-test.mjs`.\n\n```js headless\n// a game with no display, in Node or a test: fixed steps, scripted input, its state\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\nconst hero = new E.Body({ x: 40, y: 40, r: 5 });\ngame.start({ update(dt) { hero.vx = game.input.move()[0] * 80; if (game.input.pressed('jump')) hero.jump(210); hero.update(dt); }, draw() {} });\ngame.input.hold('right'); game.input.tap('jump');\ngame.advance(0.25);   // 30 fixed steps of 1/120 s, at once\nif (!(hero.x > 55 && hero.z > 20)) throw new Error('the hero should run right and be in the air');\ngame.dispose();\n```\n\n```js heights\n// a guard on a roof, a hero in the street: sight, reach and a climb read heights the same way\nconst E = My3D2dge, map = new E.TileMap({ rows: ['#######', '#.....#', '#..RR.#', '#######'], legend: { '#': 1, R: 2 }, types: { 1: { h: 80 }, 2: { h: 40 } } });\nconst guard = { x: 56, y: 40, z: 40, facing: Math.PI }, hero = { x: 36, y: 40, z: 0, r: 5 };\nif (!map.sight(guard, hero)) throw new Error('eyes on a roof see down into the street');\nif (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\nconst up = map.ledge(hero, 0);   // east, toward the roof\nif (!up || up.z !== 40) throw new Error('a ledge to climb onto the roof');\n```\n\n## Contents\n\nThe line each section starts on, and the name its classes' instances go by: `E.Attack: slash` lists its members as `slash.start`.\n\n- 108 The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n- 119 Math\n- 194 Pixel primitives\n- 213 Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n- 219 Views (projections); E.View: view\n- 246 Screen; game.screen\n- 268 Input; E.Input: input\n- 353 Pixel font\n- 364 Lighting; game.lights\n- 383 Particles; E.Particles: game.particles\n- 403 Renderer; r\n- 451 Game; E.Game: game\n- 562 Standard features; settings, fullscreen\n- 579 10c. Boot\n- 584 10d. Tweens and scripts; E.Script: script, E.Tween: tween\n- 601 10e. Paths; E.Path: path\n- 611 10g. Weather\n- 615 10k. Save slots; E.Saves: saves\n- 638 Humanoid rig; E.Attack: slash, E.Combo: combo, E.Humanoid: rig\n- 711 Blob rig; E.Blob: blob\n- 731 Tile map; E.TileMap: map\n- 794 Materials\n- 815 Flow field; E.FlowField: flow\n- 833 Texture helpers for floortex functions\n- 844 Platform map; E.PlatformMap: level\n- 878 Platformer; E.Platformer: hero\n- 919 Body; E.Body: body\n- 939 Actions; E.Action: action\n- 961 17c. Mover; E.Mover: mover\n- 1000 17d. Perception; E.Suspicion: suspicion\n- 1017 Bullets; E.Bullets: shots\n- 1037 Spatial hash; E.SpatialHash: grid\n- 1047 Audio; game.audio\n- 1079 Backdrops; E.Backdrop: backdrop\n- 1087 21c. Props\n- 1092 21e. Shapes\n- 1104 Ui; E.Dialog: talk, E.Menu: menu\n- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n- 1190 Gpu lighting (webgpu); game.gpu\n- 1211 Sessions\n- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n- 1255 Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js); E.Click: click, E.Walkbox: walkbox\n- 1300 Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engine/modules/drive.js); E.Car: car, E.Race: race\n- 1338 Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a meter; rounds; a CPU; training (engine/modules/fight.js); E.FightAI: fightai, E.FightSelect: fightselect, E.FightStage: fightstage, E.Fighter: fighter, E.Match: match\n- 1419 Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed (engine/modules/gen.js)\n- 1430 Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers and turns (engine/modules/grid.js); E.Fog: fog, E.Grid: grid, E.GridMover: gridmover, E.Turns: turns\n- 1489 Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance (engine/modules/mode7.js); E.Mode7: mode7\n- 1512 Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never pass through (engine/modules/physics.js); E.Physics: physics\n- 1541 Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway (engine/modules/rhythm.js); E.Rhythm: rhythm\n- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n- 1590 Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates and saves (engine/modules/rooms.js); E.World: world\n- 1619 Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage, encounters (engine/modules/rpg.js); E.RPG: rpg\n- 1638 Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engine/modules/songs.js)\n- 1646 Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js); E.Story: story\n- 1675 Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, resources, placement, fog, AI; a day clock, needs, overlays (engine/modules/strategy.js); E.Clock: clock, E.Strategy: strategy\n- 1721 Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in chunks (engine/modules/terrain.js); E.Terrain: terrain\n\n## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n\n- `E.DEG: 0.017453292519943295`: π/180, one degree in radians (angle * DEG)\n- `E.TAU: 6.283185307179586`: 2π, a full turn in radians\n- `E.build: \"dev-build\"`: the commit this copy was built from, a placeholder in the repo that tools/stamp.mjs replaces when the site deploys (e.g. 'a1b2c3d 2026-10-07')\n- `E.current: null`: the latest game made (My3D2dge.current, for tools and tests)\n- `E.name: \"my-3D2dge\"`: the engine's name, 'my-3D2dge'\n- `E.version: \"0.85.2\"`: the release (package.json, written everywhere by node tools/version.mjs)\n- `E.versionLabel()`: 'v0.7.0 · a1b2c3d 2026-10-07': the label to show on screens and in reports\n- `E.warn(key, msg)`: one console warning per distinct problem, prefixed so tools (and people) can spot engine advice: warn(key, message)\n\n## 1. Math","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01D6EhXqauZtbbZcYfcbtUET","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
