{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015Z5DosJjKR7dCzy6fy5EQX","type":"tool_result","content":"864\t### 4.13 HUD (canvas pixel UI; anchor to `r.W`/`r.H`; keep clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n865\t- **Top center: TIME.**\n866\t  - \"TIME\" over **`45.00`** (font scale 3), on a 90×28 plate whose water level rises as TIME runs out;\n867\t  - red below 10 s, blinking below 5 s, a tick sound each second;\n868\t  - the boss bar goes under it.\n869\t- **Top left: SCORE** (scale 2), with the chain \"×1.4\" under it.\n870\t- **Bottom left: LIFE**, a row of CREST shield-badge sprites that flash and break when lost.\n871\t- **Bottom right: the weapon panel.**\n872\t  - icon, name and ammo: 9 bullet pips for the handgun; a number and a bar for specials;\n873\t  - a reload ring while in cover;\n874\t  - a 4-slot strip shows for 0.8 s after a switch.\n875\t- **Center**:\n876\t  - the reticle in the player's color with a white outline (styles: cross, ring, dot; sizes S/M/L);\n877\t  - a hit marker (a white ×, gold for a headshot);\n878\t  - \"RELOAD!\" under the ammo and flashing over the reticle when empty;\n879\t  - **\"ACTION!\"** (scale 4, slides in, 0.9 s) and **\"WAIT\"** (scale 3, blinking);\n880\t  - \"TIME EXTEND +2\", \"TIDE'S IN!\", \"STAGE CLEAR\";\n881\t  - score popups (\"+1500\") at the projected enemy positions;\n882\t  - pickup banners (\"MACHINE GUN +60\");\n883\t  - \"NEW WEAPON\" cards the first time a weapon is picked up.\n884\t- **Threat rings and edge arrows**, as in §4.7.\n885\t- **Cover feedback**: a dark vignette, a small \"COVER\" tag at the bottom center, the reticle hidden.\n886\t- **Radio box**: at the top, with a 32-px live portrait, the name in the speaker's color, two lines of at most 40\n887\t  characters, auto-advancing.\n888\t- **Prompt bar** (bottom center): device-aware tutorial prompts the first time (\"HOLD [L2] TO TAKE COVER\").\n889\t- **Co-op**:\n890\t  - split screen: each viewport has its own HUD. Secondary text uses scale 1, but key numbers never go below scale 2.\n891\t  - AI Hub: a teammate strip at the top right (name in the seat color, lives, a ● when in cover).\n892\t- **10-foot sizes**: the smallest text is scale 1 (7 px of 240, about 31 px on a 1080p TV); key numbers are scale 2–3.\n893\t  Check 16:9, 4:3 and 21:9.\n894\t\n895\t### 4.14 Screens, flow and the 10-foot UI\n896\t**Rules**:\n897\t- at most 7 items a screen, each with a one-line description under it;\n898\t- one big focus highlight, animated as a wave;\n899\t- d-pad, stick or arrows move the focus, and hovering the mouse moves it too; ✕, Enter or a click picks; ○, Esc or a\n900\t  right click goes back;\n901\t- no dense tables: the results show 6 big count-up stats, and lists are paged (L1/R1, the wheel, or arrows), never\n902\t  scrolled.\n903\t\n904\tUse `E.Menu` (it already does hover, click and keys), drawn with our own frame (`E.ui.box`, gradient\n905\t`['#10244a', '#081428']`, accent `#3aa0e8`, text `#f4f7ff`, gold `#ffd36a`, warning `#ff3b30`).\n906\t\n907\t```\n908\tboot → title ─(any button)→ menu ─┬ ARCADE → difficulty → briefing(1) → play(1) → results → briefing(2) … → ending → initials → records → title\n909\t                                  ├ CO-OP → coop join (P2 press START on a pad) → difficulty → (as ARCADE, split screen)\n910\t                                  ├ STAGE SELECT → 3 cards → difficulty → briefing(n) → play(n) → results → initials → title\n911\t                                  ├ TRAINING → play(range) → range results → menu\n912\t                                  ├ RECORDS (tables per mode · range best · INTEL)   ├ SETTINGS (engine screens)\n913\t                                  └ ABOUT (pages)                                     └ HOW TO PLAY (device-aware diagram)\n914\tplay: pause (engine menu: Resume · Restart scene · Restart stage · How to play · Dev mode · Settings · Controls · Full screen · Quit to title)\n915\ttitle/menu idle 10 s → attract (§4.17)          AI Hub: boot → session card → play(round stage) → session results\n916\t```\n917\t**The screens**:\n918\t- **Title**: a slow flyover of Stage 1's night harbor with fireworks, rendered by Rail3D.\n919\t  - The logo is `E.font.title` \"TIDE CRISIS\" (scale 4; colors `#ffffff #9fe3ff #3aa0e8 #1a4f9c`; outline `#08142a`;\n920\t    depth 3) with a big \"3\" in `#fff3b0 #ffb347 #ff5a2a #a81e1e` and an animated wave band under it.\n921\t  - \"PRESS ✕\" for a pad, \"PRESS ENTER OR CLICK\" for keyboard and mouse.\n922\t  - `E.versionLabel()` small, at the bottom.\n923\t- **Touch-only** devices (coarse pointer, no fine pointer, no gamepad, no key pressed yet): the title shows **\"Controller\n924\t  or keyboard required\"** and a large gear button that opens `game.menu('settings')`. There are no touch controls\n925\t  (`touch: []`, `input.touchEnabled = false`). The attract mode runs. A key press or a connected pad unlocks the\n926\t  normal title.\n927\t- **Briefing**: map pages; skip with ✕ or Enter.\n928\t- **Results**: the stage name, then count-ups (time, accuracy, kills, headshots, cover saves, lives lost), the time\n929\t  bonus, the accuracy bonus (`accuracy% × 300`), the no-damage bonus (20,000) and the total. The rank letter lands\n930\t  with a shake.\n931\t- **Game over**: \"GAME OVER\" → initials on `E.Arcade`'s letter wheel if the score qualifies → the table.\n932\t- **Ending**: the cutscene, the credits roll (cast with live portraits, \"Made with my-3D2dge\", the music), the final\n933\t  score, the initials.\n934\t- **Records**: tables `arcade`, `coop`, `stage1`–`stage3` (via `E.Arcade.table/qualifies/enter/drawTable`), the range's\n935\t  best time, and INTEL (the bottles found, each with its short funny note).\n936\t- **About**, as pages:\n937\t  1. the game and its credits;\n938\t  2. **Source Information**;\n939\t  3. **Testing Feedback**;\n940\t  4. **Engine Feedback**;\n941\t  5. **Prompt Feedback**;\n942\t  6. thanks and licenses (the engine is MIT; the asset store is CC0 if used).\n943\t\n944\t  All of it comes from `src/99-about.js`.\n945\t\n946\t### 4.15 Settings (our items, added through `menu.settings` beside the engine's)\n947\t| Key | Label | Options (default) |\n948\t|---|---|---|\n949\t| `difficulty` | Difficulty (new runs) | Easy / **Normal** / Hard |\n950\t| `aimAssist` | Aim assist (controller) | Off / Low / **Medium** / High |\n951\t| `padSpeed` | Aim speed (controller) | slider 0.5–2.0 (**1.0**) |\n952\t| `coverMode` | Cover control | **Hold** / Toggle |\n953\t| `autoFire` | Hold fire to repeat (handgun) | **On** / Off |\n954\t| `reticle` / `reticleSize` | Reticle / size | **Cross** / Ring / Dot · S / **M** / L |\n955\t| `threatSize` | Crisis rings | **Normal** / Large |\n956\t| `subtitles` | Subtitles | **On** / Off |\n957\t| `wobble` | Retro texture wobble | **Off** / On |\n958\t\n959\tThe engine already provides Button symbols (patched to PlayStation by default, with Xbox), volumes, comfort settings\n960\t(shake and flashes, which our FX respect), screen filters (CRT, scanlines), dead zone, invert Y, vibration and\n961\trebinding. Its Controls screen names our actions: `menu.controls = { fire: 'Fire', cover: 'Take cover', next: 'Next weapon', prev: 'Previous weapon', reload: 'Quick reload', w1: 'Handgun', … }`.\n962\t\n963\t### 4.16 Dev mode (from the pause menu; not available in AI Hub sessions)\n964\t\"Dev mode\" in the pause menu resumes the engine and opens our **canvas dev panel**. The Sim is frozen while the panel\n965\tis open; close it to play with the new values. It has 6 tabs (L1/R1, Q/E or a click):\n966\t\n967\t1. **PLAYER**: God mode · Infinite ammo · Start lives (1–9, 5) · I-frames (0.5–3 s, 1.5) · Cover in (0.05–0.4, 0.12) ·\n968\t   Cover out (0.05–0.4, 0.15) · Reload (0.1–1.0, 0.30) · Pad aim speed (0.5–3, 1.6) · Aim assist (0–1, .6).\n969\t2. **WEAPONS**: handgun damage (0.5–3, 1) · MG rate (4–20/s, 12) · MG damage (0.1–1, .45) · shotgun pellets (4–14, 8) ·\n970\t   shotgun spread (2–12°, 5.5) · GL radius (24–96, 48) · GL damage (2–12, 6) · Ammo pickups × (0.5–3, 1).\n971\t3. **ENEMIES**: HP × (0.5–3, 1) · Threat chance × (0–3, 1) · Telegraph × (0.5–2, 1) · Fire interval × (0.5–2, 1) ·\n972\t   Max threats (1–4) · Minimum gap (0.1–1 s, .35) · Reaction delay × (0.5–2, 1) · Boss HP × (0.25–3, 1).\n973\t4. **TIME**: Freeze timer · Scene time × (0.5–2, 1) · Elite bonus (0–5 s, 2) · Refill after time-up (20–100%, 60) ·\n974\t   Game speed (0.25–1.5, 1).\n975\t5. **VIEW**: FOV (45–75, 55) · Show hit volumes · Colliders · Rail and cover points · AI state labels · Threat debug ·\n976\t   Perf overlay (ms per pass, triangles, pixels, actors) · Free camera · Hide HUD.\n977\t6. **ACTIONS**: Restart scene · Next / previous scene · Jump to… (every scene, boss and cutscene) · Kill all · Spawn\n978\t   enemy (pick a type; it appears at the nearest free cover point) · All weapons and full ammo · +1 life · Lose a life ·\n979\t   Trigger a threat on me · Clear stage · Game over · Bot plays (Autopilot) · Add a P2 bot (split-screen test) ·\n980\t   Voice test (each speaker says a line) · Music test (every song and layer).\n981\t\n982\t**RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS** sits at the bottom, with a confirmation. □ or Backspace resets the focused item.\n983\t- Changed values show in gold, with the default in grey.\n984\t- Navigation: up/down move; left/right adjust (holding accelerates); ✕ or Enter toggles or runs; ○ or Esc closes.\n985\t  Hovering the mouse focuses, dragging moves a slider's knob, and the wheel adjusts.\n986\t- Values live in `tune` for the visit, and Reset copies `TUNE` back.\n987\t- Every slider's key is a path into `tune` (`'enemy.hpMul'`), and the panel is generated from a descriptor list, so\n988\t  adding a variable takes one line.\n989\t\n990\t### 4.17 Attract mode and the Autopilot\n991\t**The attract controller** (`53-attract.js`):\n992\t- **Trigger**: 10 s on the title or the main menu with no input. Input means any key or button, a pointer move of more\n993\t  than 4 px, the wheel, or a stick past its dead zone.\n994\t- **The cycle**: DEMO (highlight *i*, about 28 s) → HIGH SCORES (6 s) → DEMO (*i+1*) → TITLE (8 s) → repeat, carrying\n995\t  on through the playlist.\n996\t- **The playlist** (`def('highlight', …)`), in order:\n997\t  1. 1-1 Lantern Pier\n998\t  2. 1-4 Canal Run\n999\t  3. 1-B Barracuda\n1000\t  4. 2-1 Gull's Rest\n1001\t  5. 2-3 Funicular and The Gull\n1002\t  6. 2-B Hammerhead\n1003\t  7. 3-2 Sluice Locks and Seawolf\n1004\t  8. 3-3 Turbine Hall\n1005\t  9. 3-B Scylla and Krake\n1006\t- **The demo** is `Sim({ mode: 'attract' })` jumped to the highlight. It cheats freely: god mode, infinite ammo, travel\n1007\t  ×1.5. Telegraphs still show, so the mechanic is visible. The bot plays in `showoff` style.\n1008\t- The overlay shows \"DEMO PLAY\", the small logo and a blinking \"PRESS START\" in the right device label. The HUD stays.\n1009\t- **Any input** goes back to the title, and that input is consumed so it doesn't also pick a menu item.\n1010\t- **Watchdog**: if nothing progresses for 8 s, move to the next highlight.\n1011\t- On touch-only devices the attract mode runs the same way; a tap goes back to the title, which shows the notice.\n1012\t\n1013\t**The Autopilot** produces the same `Command` objects a player does. It drives tests (`fair`), the attract mode\n1014\t(`showoff`) and the dev \"P2 bot\".\n1015\t- **Perception**: it reads the Sim state, including threats and their timers.\n1016\t- **Target priority**:\n1017\t  1. threats on me, soonest impact first;\n1018\t  2. projectiles in flight;\n1019\t  3. Red Tide and snipers;\n1020\t  4. rushers, nearest first;\n1021\t  5. shields, if a shotgun or GL is available;\n1022\t  6. the rest, by exposure time left.\n1023\t\n1024\t  Never civilians, hostages or allies. When idle: life rings, bottles, and barrels next to enemies.\n1025\t- **Aim**: a critically damped spring toward the target's head (headshot chance by skill) or chest, with a maximum\n1026\t  speed and a reaction delay. It fires when the projected reticle is inside the target's volume, with jitter by skill.\n1027\t- **Cover**: hide when a threat on me has under 0.25 s left and its source won't die first; hide to reload when empty\n1028\t  (or at ≤ 2 rounds with no threats); pop out when no impact is due within 0.3 s.\n1029\t- **Weapons**: MG against drones and groups; the shotgun against rushers, shields and close range; the GL against\n1030\t  vehicles, barricades and bosses' armored parts; otherwise the handgun.\n1031\t- **Skills**:\n1032\t\n1033\t| Skill | Reaction | Speed | Headshots |\n1034\t|---|---|---|---|\n1035\t| `fair` | 0.30 s | 2.2 vu/s | 30% |\n1036\t| `expert` | 0.18 s | 3.5 vu/s | 60% |\n1037\t| `showoff` | `expert`, and uses every weapon and bonus target | | |\n1038\t\n1039\t### 4.18 Local co-op (split screen)\n1040\t- **CO-OP** opens a join screen: \"PLAYER 2 — PRESS START ON A CONTROLLER\".\n1041\t  - `game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin })`; the new player is `game.addPlayer({ pad: i })`.\n1042\t  - P1 keeps the keyboard and mouse and any other pad. The mouse always belongs to P1.\n1043\t  - In ARCADE, a second pad's Start also drops P2 in during play, with a slide into split screen.\n1044\t- `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'columns' })`. Rail3D renders each viewport with that player's camera, and the HUD is\n1045\t  drawn per viewport.\n1046\t- One Sim with two players: shared enemies, time and rail; separate slots, cover, aim, weapons, ammo, lives, score\n1047\t  and continues.\n1048\t  - Threats choose a target player.\n1049\t  - Pickups go to the player who made the kill.\n1050\t  - Life rings go to whoever shoots them.\n1051\t- When a player is out, their half shows \"CONTINUE? 10\" while the other plays on. If both are out, it's game over.\n1052\t\n1053\t### 4.19 AI Hub online co-op (shared world; follow `lib/hub/README.md`, protocol 1)\n1054\t**Tags** in `<head>`, after the session client:\n1055\t```html\n1056\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1057\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1058\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1059\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Clear the stage together; most points wins\">\n1060\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim mouse/stick · Fire click/R2 · Hold right-click/L2: cover+reload\">\n1061\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"7\">\n1062\t```\n1063\tThe goal must stay at 60 characters or fewer and the howto at 80 or fewer.\n1064\t\n1065\t**Flow** when `AIHub.active`:\n1066\t1. Skip the title, the attract mode and every menu. Use `new E.Game({ autoPause: false, corner: false, fullscreen: false, … })`,\n1067\t   and make the play scene not pausable.\n1068\t2. In the first boot step, call\n1069\t   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`,\n1070\t   carry on as a normal game.\n1071\t3. Build the round's stage: **stage = ((info.round − 1) mod 3) + 1**. Seats map to agents in seat order: Kai, Rook,\n1072\t   Mari, Juno, and the colors come from `info.players`.\n1073\t4. Call `AIHub.ready()` with no key press.\n1074\t5. Show **our own card**, the session briefing: the stage name and art, every player in their color with a READY tick,\n1075\t   the goal, this device's controls, and the countdown from the `card` event.\n1076\t   - Enter or ✕ (button 0) calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n1077\t   - △ (button 3) or M calls `AIHub.answer('more')`; answering again takes it back.\n1078\t   - The card has no menus or choices, and draws no `Math.random`.\n1079\t6. On `start`, count down 3-2-1 while `AIHub.time() < 0`; ACTION! at 0. No intro cutscene.\n1080\t7. **Host** (`info.isHost`) runs the authoritative Sim with every player.\n1081\t   - **Server** (`AIHub.server`): no local player, input or camera. Show a status screen (\"HOSTING · 3 AGENTS ·\n1082\t     AREA 1-3\") and keep the world running.\n1083\t8. The end:\n1084\t   - the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })` once: on the boss's defeat, when every\n1085\t     player has left, or immediately on `time-up`;\n1086\t   - `standings` group equal scores; `won` is true if the boss was defeated;\n1087\t   - stats per player: Kills, Accuracy, Headshots, Cover saves, Lives lost;\n1088\t   - awards: Sharpshooter (best accuracy), Pointman (most kills), Iron Wall (most cover saves);\n1089\t   - on `end`: stop input (`input.clear()`, ignore everything after), `audio.stopMusic()` and mute, and show \"ROUND OVER\"\n1090\t     (or \"HOST LEFT — ROUND VOID\", or \"YOU SAT THIS ONE OUT\").\n1091\t9. **Rules**:\n1092\t   - network only through `AIHub.send`;\n1093\t   - no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation;\n1094\t   - Quit, Restart and Title do nothing;\n1095\t   - Options while Create is held is ignored;\n1096\t   - names are only ever drawn to the canvas, never into HTML.\n1097\t\n1098\t**Messages** (short keys, quantized integers):\n1099\t\n1100\t| Direction | Message | Reliability, rate | Content |\n1101\t|---|---|---|---|\n1102\t| client → host | `in` | unreliable, 15/s | `{ t: 'in', at, a: [ax·1000, ay·1000], c: 0/1, w }` |\n1103\t| client → host | `sh` | reliable, ≤ 8/s, only when something happened | shots `[[at, w, ax, ay], …]` and cover changes `[[at, c], …]` since the last |\n1104\t| host → all | `s` | unreliable, 10/s, **≤ 1,100 bytes** | `{ t: 's', at, ph, sc, d, tm, p: [[id, score, lives, chain, w, ammo, c]], e: [[id, type, x, y, z, yaw, state, hp]], pr: [[id, kind, x, y, z]], b: [phase, …hp] }` |\n1105\t| host → all | `ev` | reliable, ≤ 8/s, batched | spawn, kill (with the shooter), hit, threat (`{ id, src, target, t0, dur }` in hub time), pickup, cue, scene, clear, over |\n1106\t\n1107\t- **Rate limit**: a token bucket of 18 messages per second per copy (the protocol caps it at 20). Skip a snapshot when\n1108\t  the bucket is empty; reliable batches merge.\n1109\t- **The host**:\n1110\t  - applies each player's latest `in` and every `sh` shot, rewinding the enemies: it keeps a 300-ms ring buffer of hit\n1111\t    volumes at 30 Hz and tests each shot against the sample nearest its `at`, clamped 0–250 ms into the past;\n1112\t  - keeps a cover timeline per player;\n1113\t  - resolves each threat at T + 0.2 s against the cover state that player reported at T.\n1114\t- **The replica** (a client):\n1115\t  - renders enemies interpolated at `AIHub.time() − 120 ms`, driving rigs from position, velocity and state codes;\n1116\t  - draws threat rings from `threat` events on the hub's timeline;\n1117\t  - predicts its own cover, weapon and ammo at once and corrects them when the snapshot disagrees for 0.5 s;\n1118\t  - takes score and lives from the host;\n1119\t  - shows its own shots' sparks and hit markers at once, against the interpolated volumes, as cosmetics only; the\n1120\t    host's `kill` events decide.\n1121\t- **When a player leaves**: their agent disappears and threats retarget. If the host leaves, the clients get\n1122\t  `end: host-left`.\n1123\t- A snapshot over budget drops the enemies furthest from every camera; they come round-robin in the next snapshot.\n1124\t\n1125\t### 4.20 Records, saves and intel\n1126\t- High-score tables go through `E.Arcade` (modes `arcade`, `coop`, `stage1`–`stage3`). Don't use `E.Arcade.add`: it\n1127\t  floats points in 2D world space. Use only `table`, `qualifies`, `enter` and `drawTable`.\n1128\t- The range's best time, the flags (`seenTraining`, `seenPrompts.*`) and the INTEL bottles found (6: two per stage) go\n1129\t  in `E.store`.\n1130\t- There are no mid-run saves; this is an arcade game. STAGE SELECT makes every stage reachable.\n1131\t- In AI Hub sessions, storage is the client's memory-only storage, so nothing persists. That's fine.\n1132\t\n1133\t---\n1134\t\n1135\t## 5. Content\n1136\t\n1137\t### 5.1 World and cast\n1138\tThe **Lumen Isles** are an island republic whose capital, **Port Lumen**, lies below sea level behind the **Meridian"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"0d1cfb12-8f02-4df8-93d8-b66ea0910570","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:36:40.586Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 4.13 HUD (canvas pixel UI; anchor to `r.W`/`r.H`; keep clear of `game.cornerArea()`)\n- **Top center: TIME.**\n  - \"TIME\" over **`45.00`** (font scale 3), on a 90×28 plate whose water level rises as TIME runs out;\n  - red below 10 s, blinking below 5 s, a tick sound each second;\n  - the boss bar goes under it.\n- **Top left: SCORE** (scale 2), with the chain \"×1.4\" under it.\n- **Bottom left: LIFE**, a row of CREST shield-badge sprites that flash and break when lost.\n- **Bottom right: the weapon panel.**\n  - icon, name and ammo: 9 bullet pips for the handgun; a number and a bar for specials;\n  - a reload ring while in cover;\n  - a 4-slot strip shows for 0.8 s after a switch.\n- **Center**:\n  - the reticle in the player's color with a white outline (styles: cross, ring, dot; sizes S/M/L);\n  - a hit marker (a white ×, gold for a headshot);\n  - \"RELOAD!\" under the ammo and flashing over the reticle when empty;\n  - **\"ACTION!\"** (scale 4, slides in, 0.9 s) and **\"WAIT\"** (scale 3, blinking);\n  - \"TIME EXTEND +2\", \"TIDE'S IN!\", \"STAGE CLEAR\";\n  - score popups (\"+1500\") at the projected enemy positions;\n  - pickup banners (\"MACHINE GUN +60\");\n  - \"NEW WEAPON\" cards the first time a weapon is picked up.\n- **Threat rings and edge arrows**, as in §4.7.\n- **Cover feedback**: a dark vignette, a small \"COVER\" tag at the bottom center, the reticle hidden.\n- **Radio box**: at the top, with a 32-px live portrait, the name in the speaker's color, two lines of at most 40\n  characters, auto-advancing.\n- **Prompt bar** (bottom center): device-aware tutorial prompts the first time (\"HOLD [L2] TO TAKE COVER\").\n- **Co-op**:\n  - split screen: each viewport has its own HUD. Secondary text uses scale 1, but key numbers never go below scale 2.\n  - AI Hub: a teammate strip at the top right (name in the seat color, lives, a ● when in cover).\n- **10-foot sizes**: the smallest text is scale 1 (7 px of 240, about 31 px on a 1080p TV); key numbers are scale 2–3.\n  Check 16:9, 4:3 and 21:9.\n\n### 4.14 Screens, flow and the 10-foot UI\n**Rules**:\n- at most 7 items a screen, each with a one-line description under it;\n- one big focus highlight, animated as a wave;\n- d-pad, stick or arrows move the focus, and hovering the mouse moves it too; ✕, Enter or a click picks; ○, Esc or a\n  right click goes back;\n- no dense tables: the results show 6 big count-up stats, and lists are paged (L1/R1, the wheel, or arrows), never\n  scrolled.\n\nUse `E.Menu` (it already does hover, click and keys), drawn with our own frame (`E.ui.box`, gradient\n`['#10244a', '#081428']`, accent `#3aa0e8`, text `#f4f7ff`, gold `#ffd36a`, warning `#ff3b30`).\n\n```\nboot → title ─(any button)→ menu ─┬ ARCADE → difficulty → briefing(1) → play(1) → results → briefing(2) … → ending → initials → records → title\n                                  ├ CO-OP → coop join (P2 press START on a pad) → difficulty → (as ARCADE, split screen)\n                                  ├ STAGE SELECT → 3 cards → difficulty → briefing(n) → play(n) → results → initials → title\n                                  ├ TRAINING → play(range) → range results → menu\n                                  ├ RECORDS (tables per mode · range best · INTEL)   ├ SETTINGS (engine screens)\n                                  └ ABOUT (pages)                                     └ HOW TO PLAY (device-aware diagram)\nplay: pause (engine menu: Resume · Restart scene · Restart stage · How to play · Dev mode · Settings · Controls · Full screen · Quit to title)\ntitle/menu idle 10 s → attract (§4.17)          AI Hub: boot → session card → play(round stage) → session results\n```\n**The screens**:\n- **Title**: a slow flyover of Stage 1's night harbor with fireworks, rendered by Rail3D.\n  - The logo is `E.font.title` \"TIDE CRISIS\" (scale 4; colors `#ffffff #9fe3ff #3aa0e8 #1a4f9c`; outline `#08142a`;\n    depth 3) with a big \"3\" in `#fff3b0 #ffb347 #ff5a2a #a81e1e` and an animated wave band under it.\n  - \"PRESS ✕\" for a pad, \"PRESS ENTER OR CLICK\" for keyboard and mouse.\n  - `E.versionLabel()` small, at the bottom.\n- **Touch-only** devices (coarse pointer, no fine pointer, no gamepad, no key pressed yet): the title shows **\"Controller\n  or keyboard required\"** and a large gear button that opens `game.menu('settings')`. There are no touch controls\n  (`touch: []`, `input.touchEnabled = false`). The attract mode runs. A key press or a connected pad unlocks the\n  normal title.\n- **Briefing**: map pages; skip with ✕ or Enter.\n- **Results**: the stage name, then count-ups (time, accuracy, kills, headshots, cover saves, lives lost), the time\n  bonus, the accuracy bonus (`accuracy% × 300`), the no-damage bonus (20,000) and the total. The rank letter lands\n  with a shake.\n- **Game over**: \"GAME OVER\" → initials on `E.Arcade`'s letter wheel if the score qualifies → the table.\n- **Ending**: the cutscene, the credits roll (cast with live portraits, \"Made with my-3D2dge\", the music), the final\n  score, the initials.\n- **Records**: tables `arcade`, `coop`, `stage1`–`stage3` (via `E.Arcade.table/qualifies/enter/drawTable`), the range's\n  best time, and INTEL (the bottles found, each with its short funny note).\n- **About**, as pages:\n  1. the game and its credits;\n  2. **Source Information**;\n  3. **Testing Feedback**;\n  4. **Engine Feedback**;\n  5. **Prompt Feedback**;\n  6. thanks and licenses (the engine is MIT; the asset store is CC0 if used).\n\n  All of it comes from `src/99-about.js`.\n\n### 4.15 Settings (our items, added through `menu.settings` beside the engine's)\n| Key | Label | Options (default) |\n|---|---|---|\n| `difficulty` | Difficulty (new runs) | Easy / **Normal** / Hard |\n| `aimAssist` | Aim assist (controller) | Off / Low / **Medium** / High |\n| `padSpeed` | Aim speed (controller) | slider 0.5–2.0 (**1.0**) |\n| `coverMode` | Cover control | **Hold** / Toggle |\n| `autoFire` | Hold fire to repeat (handgun) | **On** / Off |\n| `reticle` / `reticleSize` | Reticle / size | **Cross** / Ring / Dot · S / **M** / L |\n| `threatSize` | Crisis rings | **Normal** / Large |\n| `subtitles` | Subtitles | **On** / Off |\n| `wobble` | Retro texture wobble | **Off** / On |\n\nThe engine already provides Button symbols (patched to PlayStation by default, with Xbox), volumes, comfort settings\n(shake and flashes, which our FX respect), screen filters (CRT, scanlines), dead zone, invert Y, vibration and\nrebinding. Its Controls screen names our actions: `menu.controls = { fire: 'Fire', cover: 'Take cover', next: 'Next weapon', prev: 'Previous weapon', reload: 'Quick reload', w1: 'Handgun', … }`.\n\n### 4.16 Dev mode (from the pause menu; not available in AI Hub sessions)\n\"Dev mode\" in the pause menu resumes the engine and opens our **canvas dev panel**. The Sim is frozen while the panel\nis open; close it to play with the new values. It has 6 tabs (L1/R1, Q/E or a click):\n\n1. **PLAYER**: God mode · Infinite ammo · Start lives (1–9, 5) · I-frames (0.5–3 s, 1.5) · Cover in (0.05–0.4, 0.12) ·\n   Cover out (0.05–0.4, 0.15) · Reload (0.1–1.0, 0.30) · Pad aim speed (0.5–3, 1.6) · Aim assist (0–1, .6).\n2. **WEAPONS**: handgun damage (0.5–3, 1) · MG rate (4–20/s, 12) · MG damage (0.1–1, .45) · shotgun pellets (4–14, 8) ·\n   shotgun spread (2–12°, 5.5) · GL radius (24–96, 48) · GL damage (2–12, 6) · Ammo pickups × (0.5–3, 1).\n3. **ENEMIES**: HP × (0.5–3, 1) · Threat chance × (0–3, 1) · Telegraph × (0.5–2, 1) · Fire interval × (0.5–2, 1) ·\n   Max threats (1–4) · Minimum gap (0.1–1 s, .35) · Reaction delay × (0.5–2, 1) · Boss HP × (0.25–3, 1).\n4. **TIME**: Freeze timer · Scene time × (0.5–2, 1) · Elite bonus (0–5 s, 2) · Refill after time-up (20–100%, 60) ·\n   Game speed (0.25–1.5, 1).\n5. **VIEW**: FOV (45–75, 55) · Show hit volumes · Colliders · Rail and cover points · AI state labels · Threat debug ·\n   Perf overlay (ms per pass, triangles, pixels, actors) · Free camera · Hide HUD.\n6. **ACTIONS**: Restart scene · Next / previous scene · Jump to… (every scene, boss and cutscene) · Kill all · Spawn\n   enemy (pick a type; it appears at the nearest free cover point) · All weapons and full ammo · +1 life · Lose a life ·\n   Trigger a threat on me · Clear stage · Game over · Bot plays (Autopilot) · Add a P2 bot (split-screen test) ·\n   Voice test (each speaker says a line) · Music test (every song and layer).\n\n**RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS** sits at the bottom, with a confirmation. □ or Backspace resets the focused item.\n- Changed values show in gold, with the default in grey.\n- Navigation: up/down move; left/right adjust (holding accelerates); ✕ or Enter toggles or runs; ○ or Esc closes.\n  Hovering the mouse focuses, dragging moves a slider's knob, and the wheel adjusts.\n- Values live in `tune` for the visit, and Reset copies `TUNE` back.\n- Every slider's key is a path into `tune` (`'enemy.hpMul'`), and the panel is generated from a descriptor list, so\n  adding a variable takes one line.\n\n### 4.17 Attract mode and the Autopilot\n**The attract controller** (`53-attract.js`):\n- **Trigger**: 10 s on the title or the main menu with no input. Input means any key or button, a pointer move of more\n  than 4 px, the wheel, or a stick past its dead zone.\n- **The cycle**: DEMO (highlight *i*, about 28 s) → HIGH SCORES (6 s) → DEMO (*i+1*) → TITLE (8 s) → repeat, carrying\n  on through the playlist.\n- **The playlist** (`def('highlight', …)`), in order:\n  1. 1-1 Lantern Pier\n  2. 1-4 Canal Run\n  3. 1-B Barracuda\n  4. 2-1 Gull's Rest\n  5. 2-3 Funicular and The Gull\n  6. 2-B Hammerhead\n  7. 3-2 Sluice Locks and Seawolf\n  8. 3-3 Turbine Hall\n  9. 3-B Scylla and Krake\n- **The demo** is `Sim({ mode: 'attract' })` jumped to the highlight. It cheats freely: god mode, infinite ammo, travel\n  ×1.5. Telegraphs still show, so the mechanic is visible. The bot plays in `showoff` style.\n- The overlay shows \"DEMO PLAY\", the small logo and a blinking \"PRESS START\" in the right device label. The HUD stays.\n- **Any input** goes back to the title, and that input is consumed so it doesn't also pick a menu item.\n- **Watchdog**: if nothing progresses for 8 s, move to the next highlight.\n- On touch-only devices the attract mode runs the same way; a tap goes back to the title, which shows the notice.\n\n**The Autopilot** produces the same `Command` objects a player does. It drives tests (`fair`), the attract mode\n(`showoff`) and the dev \"P2 bot\".\n- **Perception**: it reads the Sim state, including threats and their timers.\n- **Target priority**:\n  1. threats on me, soonest impact first;\n  2. projectiles in flight;\n  3. Red Tide and snipers;\n  4. rushers, nearest first;\n  5. shields, if a shotgun or GL is available;\n  6. the rest, by exposure time left.\n\n  Never civilians, hostages or allies. When idle: life rings, bottles, and barrels next to enemies.\n- **Aim**: a critically damped spring toward the target's head (headshot chance by skill) or chest, with a maximum\n  speed and a reaction delay. It fires when the projected reticle is inside the target's volume, with jitter by skill.\n- **Cover**: hide when a threat on me has under 0.25 s left and its source won't die first; hide to reload when empty\n  (or at ≤ 2 rounds with no threats); pop out when no impact is due within 0.3 s.\n- **Weapons**: MG against drones and groups; the shotgun against rushers, shields and close range; the GL against\n  vehicles, barricades and bosses' armored parts; otherwise the handgun.\n- **Skills**:\n\n| Skill | Reaction | Speed | Headshots |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `fair` | 0.30 s | 2.2 vu/s | 30% |\n| `expert` | 0.18 s | 3.5 vu/s | 60% |\n| `showoff` | `expert`, and uses every weapon and bonus target | | |\n\n### 4.18 Local co-op (split screen)\n- **CO-OP** opens a join screen: \"PLAYER 2 — PRESS START ON A CONTROLLER\".\n  - `game.allowJoin({ max: 2, onJoin })`; the new player is `game.addPlayer({ pad: i })`.\n  - P1 keeps the keyboard and mouse and any other pad. The mouse always belongs to P1.\n  - In ARCADE, a second pad's Start also drops P2 in during play, with a slide into split screen.\n- `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'columns' })`. Rail3D renders each viewport with that player's camera, and the HUD is\n  drawn per viewport.\n- One Sim with two players: shared enemies, time and rail; separate slots, cover, aim, weapons, ammo, lives, score\n  and continues.\n  - Threats choose a target player.\n  - Pickups go to the player who made the kill.\n  - Life rings go to whoever shoots them.\n- When a player is out, their half shows \"CONTINUE? 10\" while the other plays on. If both are out, it's game over.\n\n### 4.19 AI Hub online co-op (shared world; follow `lib/hub/README.md`, protocol 1)\n**Tags** in `<head>`, after the session client:\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Clear the stage together; most points wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Aim mouse/stick · Fire click/R2 · Hold right-click/L2: cover+reload\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"7\">\n```\nThe goal must stay at 60 characters or fewer and the howto at 80 or fewer.\n\n**Flow** when `AIHub.active`:\n1. Skip the title, the attract mode and every menu. Use `new E.Game({ autoPause: false, corner: false, fullscreen: false, … })`,\n   and make the play scene not pausable.\n2. In the first boot step, call\n   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`,\n   carry on as a normal game.\n3. Build the round's stage: **stage = ((info.round − 1) mod 3) + 1**. Seats map to agents in seat order: Kai, Rook,\n   Mari, Juno, and the colors come from `info.players`.\n4. Call `AIHub.ready()` with no key press.\n5. Show **our own card**, the session briefing: the stage name and art, every player in their color with a READY tick,\n   the goal, this device's controls, and the countdown from the `card` event.\n   - Enter or ✕ (button 0) calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n   - △ (button 3) or M calls `AIHub.answer('more')`; answering again takes it back.\n   - The card has no menus or choices, and draws no `Math.random`.\n6. On `start`, count down 3-2-1 while `AIHub.time() < 0`; ACTION! at 0. No intro cutscene.\n7. **Host** (`info.isHost`) runs the authoritative Sim with every player.\n   - **Server** (`AIHub.server`): no local player, input or camera. Show a status screen (\"HOSTING · 3 AGENTS ·\n     AREA 1-3\") and keep the world running.\n8. The end:\n   - the host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })` once: on the boss's defeat, when every\n     player has left, or immediately on `time-up`;\n   - `standings` group equal scores; `won` is true if the boss was defeated;\n   - stats per player: Kills, Accuracy, Headshots, Cover saves, Lives lost;\n   - awards: Sharpshooter (best accuracy), Pointman (most kills), Iron Wall (most cover saves);\n   - on `end`: stop input (`input.clear()`, ignore everything after), `audio.stopMusic()` and mute, and show \"ROUND OVER\"\n     (or \"HOST LEFT — ROUND VOID\", or \"YOU SAT THIS ONE OUT\").\n9. **Rules**:\n   - network only through `AIHub.send`;\n   - no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `window.open` or navigation;\n   - Quit, Restart and Title do nothing;\n   - Options while Create is held is ignored;\n   - names are only ever drawn to the canvas, never into HTML.\n\n**Messages** (short keys, quantized integers):\n\n| Direction | Message | Reliability, rate | Content |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| client → host | `in` | unreliable, 15/s | `{ t: 'in', at, a: [ax·1000, ay·1000], c: 0/1, w }` |\n| client → host | `sh` | reliable, ≤ 8/s, only when something happened | shots `[[at, w, ax, ay], …]` and cover changes `[[at, c], …]` since the last |\n| host → all | `s` | unreliable, 10/s, **≤ 1,100 bytes** | `{ t: 's', at, ph, sc, d, tm, p: [[id, score, lives, chain, w, ammo, c]], e: [[id, type, x, y, z, yaw, state, hp]], pr: [[id, kind, x, y, z]], b: [phase, …hp] }` |\n| host → all | `ev` | reliable, ≤ 8/s, batched | spawn, kill (with the shooter), hit, threat (`{ id, src, target, t0, dur }` in hub time), pickup, cue, scene, clear, over |\n\n- **Rate limit**: a token bucket of 18 messages per second per copy (the protocol caps it at 20). Skip a snapshot when\n  the bucket is empty; reliable batches merge.\n- **The host**:\n  - applies each player's latest `in` and every `sh` shot, rewinding the enemies: it keeps a 300-ms ring buffer of hit\n    volumes at 30 Hz and tests each shot against the sample nearest its `at`, clamped 0–250 ms into the past;\n  - keeps a cover timeline per player;\n  - resolves each threat at T + 0.2 s against the cover state that player reported at T.\n- **The replica** (a client):\n  - renders enemies interpolated at `AIHub.time() − 120 ms`, driving rigs from position, velocity and state codes;\n  - draws threat rings from `threat` events on the hub's timeline;\n  - predicts its own cover, weapon and ammo at once and corrects them when the snapshot disagrees for 0.5 s;\n  - takes score and lives from the host;\n  - shows its own shots' sparks and hit markers at once, against the interpolated volumes, as cosmetics only; the\n    host's `kill` events decide.\n- **When a player leaves**: their agent disappears and threats retarget. If the host leaves, the clients get\n  `end: host-left`.\n- A snapshot over budget drops the enemies furthest from every camera; they come round-robin in the next snapshot.\n\n### 4.20 Records, saves and intel\n- High-score tables go through `E.Arcade` (modes `arcade`, `coop`, `stage1`–`stage3`). Don't use `E.Arcade.add`: it\n  floats points in 2D world space. Use only `table`, `qualifies`, `enter` and `drawTable`.\n- The range's best time, the flags (`seenTraining`, `seenPrompts.*`) and the INTEL bottles found (6: two per stage) go\n  in `E.store`.\n- There are no mid-run saves; this is an arcade game. STAGE SELECT makes every stage reachable.\n- In AI Hub sessions, storage is the client's memory-only storage, so nothing persists. That's fine.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Content\n\n### 5.1 World and cast\nThe **Lumen Isles** are an island republic whose capital, **Port Lumen**, lies below sea level behind the **Meridian","numLines":275,"startLine":864,"totalLines":1671}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015Z5DosJjKR7dCzy6fy5EQX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
