{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2n4tHHKNxg8Pu1fcj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The engine's `E.Arcade` and `E.store` cover the records and high-score tables. The plan's records choices are sound, so I'll use them.\n\nI'll write the design down first so it survives context summaries."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":127866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"2335947c-3d9f-4c6e-860a-274e68c66f8f","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:44.492Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2n4cedJE548oW2rz6L"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2n4tHHKNxg8Pu1fcj3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018i6YFQxW9rzauxPKap6VJ4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work/SublimeCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-183312/NOTES.md","content":"# Sublime Crisis 3: working notes\n\nSource: Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech). Original game: an on-rails first-person light-gun shooter with a cover\npedal, four weapons and a \"crisis flash\" telegraph. Title: Sublime Crisis 3 (RNG draw 12 of 50).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `engine/my-3d2dge.js`  handoff v0.85.2 engine (patched; see `engine/PATCHES.md`)\n- `hub/session.js`        AI Hub client 1.4.0, unmodified\n- `src/*.js`              the game as ordered fragments in one IIFE (concatenated by `tools/build.mjs`)\n- `tests/run.mjs`         THE test command (prints failures and one count line)\n- `tools/build.mjs`       bundles the single HTML into the work folder root and writes exit-interview.json\n- `index.html`            dev page (engine + src loaded one by one)\n\n## Architecture (as built)\n\n- `Sim` (src/60-sim.js) holds all game state and steps it deterministically from per-player commands\n  (`aim`, `fire`, `cover`, `reload`, `weapon`). Presentation only reads it. No Math.random in the sim.\n- Rendering: `Rail3D` (src/04-rail3d.js), a software z-buffer triangle rasterizer drawn into a low-res buffer,\n  with banded light and fog. Enemies are engine `E.Humanoid` rigs drawn as billboards with `rig.draw`.\n- Dynamic boss parts are boxes transformed per frame.\n- Multiplayer: host runs the Sim; clients send `in`/`sh` messages and render `s`/`ev` snapshots (protocol in\n  lib/hub/README.md, shared-world mode).\n\n## Decisions and cuts (see final report for the full list)\n\n- Title chosen by RNG: \"Sublime Crisis 3\" (draw 12 of 50 from a list kept outside the deliverable).\n- Stage and scene structure as in the plan, reduced: 3 stages of 3 areas plus a boss each; a training range.\n- Carriers (moving boat/tram rides) are cut: scenes are static on the rail.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":127866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"e959f55d-db0f-4838-ae4f-03404b74a071","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:48.271Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2n4cedJE548oW2rz6L","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018i6YFQxW9rzauxPKap6VJ4":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261103-183312__xf5fb84/work/SublimeCrisis3-TimeCrisis3-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261103-183312/NOTES.md","content":"# Sublime Crisis 3: working notes\n\nSource: Time Crisis 3 (Namco/Nextech). Original game: an on-rails first-person light-gun shooter with a cover\npedal, four weapons and a \"crisis flash\" telegraph. Title: Sublime Crisis 3 (RNG draw 12 of 50).\n\n## Layout\n\n- `engine/my-3d2dge.js`  handoff v0.85.2 engine (patched; see `engine/PATCHES.md`)\n- `hub/session.js`        AI Hub client 1.4.0, unmodified\n- `src/*.js`              the game as ordered fragments in one IIFE (concatenated by `tools/build.mjs`)\n- `tests/run.mjs`         THE test command (prints failures and one count line)\n- `tools/build.mjs`       bundles the single HTML into the work folder root and writes exit-interview.json\n- `index.html`            dev page (engine + src loaded one by one)\n\n## Architecture (as built)\n\n- `Sim` (src/60-sim.js) holds all game state and steps it deterministically from per-player commands\n  (`aim`, `fire`, `cover`, `reload`, `weapon`). Presentation only reads it. No Math.random in the sim.\n- Rendering: `Rail3D` (src/04-rail3d.js), a software z-buffer triangle rasterizer drawn into a low-res buffer,\n  with banded light and fog. Enemies are engine `E.Humanoid` rigs drawn as billboards with `rig.draw`.\n- Dynamic boss parts are boxes transformed per frame.\n- Multiplayer: host runs the Sim; clients send `in`/`sh` messages and render `s`/`ev` snapshots (protocol in\n  lib/hub/README.md, shared-world mode).\n\n## Decisions and cuts (see final report for the full list)\n\n- Title chosen by RNG: \"Sublime Crisis 3\" (draw 12 of 50 from a list kept outside the deliverable).\n- Stage and scene structure as in the plan, reduced: 3 stages of 3 areas plus a boss each; a training range.\n- Carriers (moving boat/tram rides) are cut: scenes are static on the rail.\n"}}}
