{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5i7U3WMaQrpFzPMa3G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I closed three more of the cuts this turn, but I can't honestly mark the goal complete yet. Carriers are still unbuilt, and I haven't checked the enemy roster against the plan's full list.\n\n**Built this turn**\n- **Mouse-wheel weapon switching:** a second engine patch (in `engine/PATCHES.md`). Wheel notches press `WheelUp` and `WheelDown` for one step, and those are bound to previous and next weapon.\n- **Performance readout:** a dev-panel toggle showing frame time, FPS, and enemy, threat, box and projectile counts.\n- **Online cover prediction:** a client's own cover now moves at the sim's speeds, so it responds at once. Other players' cover still arrives in the host's snapshots.\n\n**Verification**\n- Default suite: 126 checks pass.\n- Browser suite (smoke, screen flow, phone emulation, dev overlays): 130 checks pass.\n- AI Hub harness (2 players, 4 players on a lossy network, host leaving, server-only): all pass.\n\n**Still open**\n- **Moving carriers** (the boat and tram rides) are not built. They're in PLAN.md's stage design, not in TASK.md. I'd build them next if you want full plan coverage.\n- **Enemy roster:** the build has seven types. I haven't compared these against PLAN.md §5.3, so I can't say whether they match.\n\n**Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` is generated from the same About data as the in-game About screens. It parses and answers every field. Its engine-feedback answer now reflects both engine patches.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:33:12\n- Source: Time Crisis 3 (Namco and Nextech; arcade 2002–2003, PlayStation 2 2003)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system\n- Perspective: first person on a rail; cover is real geometry lowered by about 12 u\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (two patches); a custom software rasterizer in JavaScript; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Playwright 1.63.0 for tests only\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel style, with procedural textures, banded light and dithered fog\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rigs (crouch, point, hurt, down, die, run), drawn as billboards\n- Audio: chip-synth music and effects written in code, with Animalese voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players\n- Testing: headless sim, hub and build suites; the Autopilot playthrough; Chromium smoke, screen flow, phone emulation and dev overlays; the AI Hub harness\n- Research: engine handoff docs, the AI Hub protocol README, and PLAN.md's planning notes\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 through Playwright 1.63.0\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown (no token or cost figures were reported during the run)\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 10 real defects. Three were game-breaking: the page never called its start function; areas cleared with no kills because the alive count was stale; AI Hub rounds were voided because the play was never registered. The rest included a shared event name overwritten, enemies hidden by their own wall, civilians blocking the clear, the Autopilot never shooting boss turrets, the server copy staying silent, and the HUD showing on the title.\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless suite that plays whole stages with the Autopilot. It caught the clear and civilian bugs and proved progression.\n- **Least helpful:** the exit-interview checks only confirm answers are present, not that they're true. Screenshot review was a sample of about four images.\n- **Not tested on real hardware:** a real phone (the notice was checked with emulation), a real gamepad (none attached), and the Xbox glyph option.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the Humanoid rigs and `rig.draw` from any `E.View`. They work as billboards and run headless.\n- **Guessed or got stuck:** the billboard facing (I matched the view's yaw convention by eye); the engine had no wheel codes, so I added them.\n- **Built myself:** the 3D layer (rasterizer, banded light and fog, the camera), plus the cover, threat and netcode logic.\n- **Hardest part:** finding exact signatures. The index and guide together are over 300 KB, and the core file is 1.2 MB.\n- **Engine changes:** the Button symbols default is now PlayStation, with Xbox second, because TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs and the engine defaulted to auto. The mouse wheel now emits WheelUp and WheelDown codes. Both are in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n- **Would change:** a one-page frame-order and scene-lifecycle overview with a minimal example per module.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked:** the explicit deliverables table, the exact file names, the AI Hub protocol link with its harness, and the no-stubs rule.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is written for a different run (a different title, folder and model), and TASK.md's RNG title rule conflicted with it.\n- **Hardest:** the scope. The plan asks for several thousand lines of features with no must-have or stretch split and no time budget.\n- **Would change:** mark features as must-have or stretch, make the plan's naming match the run, and state a budget up front."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":511740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1056},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"addb907e-3ef0-4c89-b286-9513b013509a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:15:30.437Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh5i79wPShvaiaCidwUp"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The stopping condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented with no stubs or reductions. The last assistant message states 'I can't honestly mark the goal complete yet' and lists unbuilt items: 'Moving carriers (the boat and tram rides) are not built' and 'the build has seven types' of enemy roster, not yet compared to the plan. The bundled HTML, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections are present, but feature completeness is explicitly unmet by the agent's own account."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"e1760f9f-c6af-4f1a-96ea-99f771c1a4d5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:15:32.006Z","isSynthetic":true}
