{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K9MAhKBp84s5Er68ZkBpsY","type":"tool_result","content":"### 5.4 Stage 1, HARBOR LIGHTS (Port Lumen Docks, 23:40, Lantern Festival)\n**Look**:\n- night blue; the sky goes `#0b1026 → #1b2a52 → #3a3060` with a magenta city glow at the horizon; fog `#1a2242`\n  400–2000;\n- warm paper lanterns (`#ffb347`, static lights of radius 90);\n- festival string lights (emissive `#ff5a5a #ffd34a #5ad1ff #8aff8a`);\n- fireworks bursting over the bay, each flash a dynamic light;\n- dark water with lantern sparkles.\n\nMusic: \"Harbor Lights\".\n\n| Scene | Time | Setting and cover | Waves (about 8–14 enemies) | New in this scene | Objects and cues |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **1-0 intro** | — | Mari's speedboat races in under fireworks; Krake's broadcast plays on the festival's giant screens (a live portrait texture); they dock at Lantern Pier | — | — | lines in §5.9 |\n| **1-1 LANTERN PIER** | 45 | A 7.5-m wooden pier lined with lantern stalls; the warehouses of the quay ahead (x 380). P1 hides behind stacked fish crates, P2 behind barrels and a bollard (the schema example in §4.10) | (a) 3 deckhands pop up behind stalls; (b) one comes out of the warehouse door, one jumps off a fishing boat's \n| **1-2 FISH MARKET** | 50 | Travel: along the quay, then Rook kicks in a side door. Inside, a brick hall with a tiled floor, wooden stalls, ice tables, hanging paper lanterns and an upper gallery | (a) 4 deckhands, 2 of them on the gallery, who fall when killed; (b) **the first Red Tide** rolls out from behind the ice table; (c\n| **1-3 CONTAINER YARD** | 60 | Berth 9: container stacks (red, blue, ochre, green), a gantry crane, sodium lamps, forklifts | (a) 3 deckhands jump down off containers and 2 hide behind forklifts; (b) **BULLDOG**, an armored truck, smashes through a container wall: its gunner (3 HP, above the gun shield, 50% threat), then its fu\n| **1-4 CANAL RUN** (moving) | 60 | Mari drives through the Silver Canals under festival bridges; duck behind the boat's armored gunwale (part of the carrier); spray, sway | 3 pairs of jet skis from side canals; bridge gunners on 2 bridges, with deckhands on the railings who fall into the water; a quartermaster on a moored boat \n| **1-B BOSS: STINGRAY → BARRACUDA** | 100 | The harbor mouth, the two boats side by side; cover behind the gunwale | §5.7 | the boss framework, torpedoes | — |\n| **1-Z outro** | — | Barracuda falls into the sea; the Stingray explodes; Juno traces Krake's signal | — | — | STAGE CLEAR → results |\n\n### 5.5 Stage 2, STORM SIGNAL (Gull's Rest and Lighthouse Point, 02:10, thunderstorm)\n**Look**:\n- slate and green-grey, with heavy rain (screen streaks and splashes);\n- lightning every 9–15 s: the sky flashes, a white `game.flash` at 0.25, thunder after 0.5–1.5 s;\n- fog `#26343c` 200–1200;\n- timber and plaster houses with slate roofs; wet stone (a `wet` overlay pattern that brightens lit bands);\n- fishermen in yellow raincoats;\n- the lighthouse beam sweeps every 8 s: a visible cone of glowing lines and a dynamic light.\n\nMusic: \"Storm Signal\".\n\n| Scene | Time | Setting and cover | Waves | New | Objects and cues |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **2-0 intro** | — | The boat docks in the rain; lightning shows the lighthouse; Krake's radio intercept and Hammerhead's reply | — | — | — |\n| **2-1 GULL'S REST** | 50 | A steep cobbled lane, timber houses, washing lines, boats up on blocks; cover behind a fish cart and a stone well | (a) deckhands in windows (the glass breaks); (b) **rushers**, 2 then 3, sprinting down the lane; (c) a quartermaster from an alley drops the **SHOTGUN +8** (\"NEW WEAPON\"); marines behin\n| **2-2 NET LOFTS** | 55 | Inside a tall wooden loft: stairs, hanging nets (`alphaTest`), fish-oil barrels | (a) a **shield** trooper advances down the stairs (\"Shotgun! Knock that shield aside!\"); (b) 3 **rappellers** drop through a roof hatch; (c) 2 Red Tide and a grenadier on the upper floor | shields, rappelling | the fish-o\n| **2-3 FUNICULAR** (moving) | 60 | The cliff funicular climbs through the storm; duck behind the car's bench and bulkhead | deckhands on the cliff-path terraces; **the passing car**: the descending car crosses with 3 gunners in a 4-s window; at the top station the car stops for **THE GULL**: a laser sniper among 3 perches on th\n| **2-4 LIGHTHOUSE KEEP** | 60 | The courtyard, the keeper's house, the lighthouse door; then up the **spiral stairs** (vertical travel; shoot upward) | (a) marines and a Red Tide; (b) **hostage**: a captor holds Dr. Tejada at the door (\"One more step and the old man swims!\"); his head shows for 0.7-s windows; (c) rushers and de\n| **2-B BOSS: HAMMERHEAD** | 120 | The lantern gallery at the top: the giant rotating lens, the storm, cover in the doorway and then behind the lens housing | §5.7 | cover that degrades and a scripted cover swap | — |\n| **2-Z outro** | — | Dr. Tejada reveals the override is in the control tower; Juno: take the maintenance tram | — | — | results |\n\n### 5.6 Stage 3, THE TIDEWALL (05:20 → 06:00, dawn)\n**Look**:\n- dawn: violet, then orange; the sky goes `#1f1a3a → #6a3f6f → #f29e6b` and the sun rises over the stage; fog\n  `#8a7a8f` 500–2400;\n- concrete slab, steel, hazard stripes (`#f2c12e`/`#1b1b1b`), sodium lamps (`#ffb04a`);\n- teal water that **rises** through the stage: the water z goes up 1.5 u per scene and 4 u in the final fight;\n- white foam at the sluices; the turbine hall's emissive screens (`#43f0c8`).\n\nMusic: \"Tidewall\".\n\n| Scene | Time | Setting and cover | Waves | New | Objects and cues |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **3-0 intro** | — | The maintenance tram runs along the crest, the sea high on one side and the city low on the other; Krake on the barrier's giant screens | — | — | — |\n| **3-1 CREST ROAD** | 50 | The crest road, gate-machinery houses, lamp posts, a barricade | (a) a swarm of 5 **drones** (\"Use the machine gun!\"); (b) 2 **rocketeers** on gantries (\"Rocket! Shoot it down!\"); (c) a quartermaster drops the **GRENADE LAUNCHER +2**; marines and a shield behind a barricade (GL blasts it apart) | dron\n| **3-2 SLUICE LOCKS** | 70 | Catwalks over the roaring sluices; the giant gate | **4 glowing gate locks**, 6 HP each, to jam before the tide gauge peaks (a scene-local gauge); **SEAWOLF**, a gunship helicopter, strafes (threat bursts), drops rappellers and retreats after 30 damage; deckhands and Red Tide on the catwalks; drones\n| **3-3 TURBINE HALL** | 60 | An interior: spinning turbines (dynamic meshes), steam vents, cranes, catwalks | (a) marines and Red Tide on catwalks; (b) 2 shields and rushers; (c) a grenadier and a rocketeer | combinations of everything | coolant tanks (explosive, white vapor); an **intel bottle**; Rook across the hall |\n| **3-4 TOWER LIFT** (moving) | 50 | The glass elevator on the outside of the control tower; duck behind the lift's console | drones; rappellers on the lift roof; **SEAWOLF returns**: 2 weapon pods (10 HP each), then the rotor hub (15 HP), and it crashes into the sea | — | the **life ring** on the lift |\n| **3-B FINAL: SCYLLA → KRAKE** | 90 + 90 | The tower roof and helipad (behind a concrete parapet), then the control room (behind the consoles) | §5.7 | the **FINAL SHOT** | — |\n| **3-Z ending** | — | The gates close, the sunrise floods in, Krake is arrested, then the credits | — | — | the ending and the credits roll |\n\n### 5.7 Bosses (patterns)\n**STINGRAY → BARRACUDA** (1-B, 100 s):\n1. **The Stingray, 100% → 60%.** The gunboat runs alongside, 25–40 m off and bobbing. Two deck turrets (12 HP each)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"4daff528-eedc-4768-8670-ed672c922a29","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:21:16.578Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### 5.4 Stage 1, HARBOR LIGHTS (Port Lumen Docks, 23:40, Lantern Festival)\n**Look**:\n- night blue; the sky goes `#0b1026 → #1b2a52 → #3a