{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh6JBaHi4Jm8xLSzFZio","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've now built the remaining PLAN.md items I could, and all 144 checks pass across the headless, browser and AI Hub suites. The goal still isn't complete, and the reason is the stage layouts, which I describe below.\n\n**Built in this round**\n- **Captor hostage:** a hostage stands beside the captor. Shooting it costs a life and 5,000 points, and the captor stays up.\n- **Jet-ski ski explosion:** killing a rider gives a 1,000-point bonus and an area blast.\n- **Drone and jet-ski meshes:** the drone is drawn as a quadrotor body with four rotor arms and a red eye, and has no human rig. The jet-ski has a ski under its rider.\n- **Entries:** jump and rappel drop onto the nest, vault arcs over the wall, and door keeps the enemy hidden until it steps out. Each is used in a real area.\n- **Boat deck:** a deck appears under the cover walls during the rail ride. Enemies still don't ride it.\n\n**Still not complete**\n- **Stage layouts:** PLAN.md §5.4–5.7 describes intro and outro scenes, several moving scenes (canal run, funicular, tower lift), and bosses with multiple phases (Stingray, Barracuda, Hammerhead, Seawolf, Scylla, Krake). It also specifies lightning, rising water, per-area objects and cues. My stages have four areas each, one ride, and simplified bosses. Matching the plan means rewriting the stage content, which I can't finish honestly in this session.\n- **Enemies riding carriers:** not built. Only the camera moves on the ride.\n\n**Deliverables:** the single HTML and `exit-interview.json` are current in the work folder root. The exit interview parses and answers every field.\n\n**Decision needed:** should I rewrite the stage content to match PLAN.md §5.4–5.7 in full, or treat TASK.md as the completion bar? The plan rewrite is the large item.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-03 18:33:12\n- Source: Time Crisis 3 (Namco and Nextech; arcade 2002–2003, PlayStation 2 2003)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre: on-rails light-gun shooter with a cover system\n- Perspective: first person on a rail; cover is real geometry lowered by about 12 u\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (two patches); a custom software rasterizer in JavaScript; AI Hub client 1.4.0; Playwright 1.63.0 for tests only\n- Art direction: the engine's PS1-era pixel style, with procedural textures, banded light and dithered fog\n- Animation: the engine's Humanoid rigs (crouch, point, hurt, down, die, run), drawn as billboards\n- Audio: chip-synth music and effects written in code, with Animalese voices\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, shared world, 1–4 players\n- Testing: headless sim, hub and build suites; the Autopilot playthrough; Chromium smoke, screen flow, phone emulation and dev overlays; the AI Hub harness\n- Research: engine handoff docs, the AI Hub protocol README, and PLAN.md's planning notes\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux under WSL2; Chromium 153 through Playwright 1.63.0\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown (no token or cost figures were reported during the run)\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 10 real defects, three of them game-breaking (the page never started; areas cleared without kills; AI Hub rounds were voided). This round a stage-2 stall came from the bot aiming too low for the drone.\n- **Most helpful test:** the headless whole-stage Autopilot playthrough.\n- **Least helpful:** the exit-interview checks, which only confirm answers are present.\n- **Not tested on real hardware:** a phone (emulated only), a gamepad, and the Xbox glyph option.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the Humanoid rigs and `rig.draw` from any view; they work as billboards and run headless.\n- **Got stuck:** the billboard facing (matched by eye); the engine had no wheel codes, so I added them.\n- **Built myself:** the software rasterizer and camera, plus the cover, threat, ride, entry and netcode logic.\n- **Changes:** PlayStation glyphs by default and mouse-wheel codes, both in `engine/PATCHES.md`.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked:** the deliverables table, exact file names, the AI Hub protocol link with its harness, and the no-stubs rule.\n- **Confusing:** PLAN.md is written for a different run (title, folder and model), which conflicted with TASK.md.\n- **Hardest:** the scope, which has no must-have or stretch split and no time budget. The stage layouts are the largest unfinished part.\n- **Would change:** mark must-have and stretch features, match the plan's naming to the run, and set a budget."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":572931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4347fe7-6622-4d1f-b2e4-5b62026e02e2","uuid":"a84be57f-d4d5-4f09-9bbf-97c1066fe860","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:23:13.891Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh6JBGShLu6smn8fU3oa"}
